# Reviewed NWScript -> Glyph binding manifest. The generator inspects the referenced NWN.Core assembly.
# function|NWScript member|Glyph name|pure/action/command/manual/exclude/deferred|return semantic type|parameter rules|receiver|aliases|category|manual adapter class|documentation/reason|deprecation
# Parameter rules: nativeName:GlyphType:pinName. Empty means infer scalar type/name; omit is allowed only for optional parameters.
# command injects an explicit Object actor and uses NWScript.AssignCommand. No delegate becomes a Glyph value.
# manual entries reuse an explicitly registered descriptor; no second wrapper is emitted.
# domain|native constant prefix|Glyph namespace. Longest prefix wins. Unselected methods/constants remain visible in coverage.
function|ActionAttack|nwn.action_attack|command||bPassive:Bool|action_attack||Actions||Attack oAttackee. - bPassive: If this is TRUE, attack is in passive mode.|
function|ActionCastFakeSpellAtLocation|nwn.action_cast_fake_spell_at_location|command||lTarget:Location|action_cast_fake_spell_at_location||Actions||The action subject will fake casting a spell at lLocation; the conjure and cast animations and visuals will occur, nothing else. - nSpell - lTarget - nProjectilePathType: PROJECTILE_PATH_TYPE_*|
function|ActionCastFakeSpellAtObject|nwn.action_cast_fake_spell_at_object|command|||action_cast_fake_spell_at_object||Actions||The action subject will fake casting a spell at oTarget; the conjure and cast animations and visuals will occur, nothing else. - nSpell - oTarget - nProjectilePathType: PROJECTILE_PATH_TYPE_*|
function|ActionCastSpellAtLocation|nwn.action_cast_spell_at_location|command||lTargetLocation:Location,bCheat:Bool,bInstantSpell:Bool,bSpontaneousCast:Bool|action_cast_spell_at_location||Actions||Cast spell nSpell at lTargetLocation. - nSpell: SPELL_* - lTargetLocation - nMetaMagic: METAMAGIC_*. If nClass is specified, cannot be METAMAGIC_ANY. - bCheat: If this is TRUE, then the executor of the action doesn't have to be able to cast the spell. Ignored if nClass is specified. - bCheat: If this is TRUE, then the executor of the action doesn't have to be able to cast the spell. - nProjectilePathType: PROJECTILE_PATH_TYPE_* - bInstantSpell: If this is TRUE, the spell is cast immediately; this allows the end-user to simulate a high-level magic user having lots of advance warning of impending trouble. - nClass: If set to a CLASS_TYPE_* it will cast using that class specifically. CLASS_TYPE_INVALID will use spell abilities. - bSpontaneousCast: If set to TRUE will attempt to cast the given spell spontaneously, ie a Cleric casting Cure Light Wounds using any level 1 slot. Needs a valid nClass set. - nDomainLevel: The level of the spell if cast from a domain slot. eg SPELL_HEAL can be spell level 5 on a cleric. Use 0 for no domain slot.|
function|ActionCastSpellAtObject|nwn.action_cast_spell_at_object|command||bCheat:Bool,bInstantSpell:Bool,bSpontaneousCast:Bool|action_cast_spell_at_object||Actions||This action casts a spell at oTarget. - nSpell: SPELL_* - oTarget: Target for the spell - nMetaMagic: METAMAGIC_*. If nClass is specified, cannot be METAMAGIC_ANY. - bCheat: If this is TRUE, then the executor of the action doesn't have to be able to cast the spell. Ignored if nClass is specified. - bCheat: If this is TRUE, then the executor of the action doesn't have to be able to cast the spell. - nDomainLevel: The level of the spell if cast from a domain slot. eg SPELL_HEAL can be spell level 5 on a cleric. Use 0 for no domain slot. - nProjectilePathType: PROJECTILE_PATH_TYPE_* - bInstantSpell: If this is TRUE, the spell is cast immediately. This allows the end-user to simulate a high-level magic-user having lots of advance warning of impending trouble - nClass: If set to a CLASS_TYPE_* it will cast using that class specifically. CLASS_TYPE_INVALID will use spell abilities. - bSpontaneousCast: If set to TRUE will attempt to cast the given spell spontaneously, ie a Cleric casting Cure Light Wounds using any level 1 slot. Needs a valid nClass set.|
function|ActionCloseDoor|nwn.action_close_door|command||bRun:Bool|action_close_door||Actions||Cause the action subject to close oDoor - bRun: If TRUE, subject will run to the door instead of walking|
function|ActionCounterSpell|nwn.action_counter_spell|command|||action_counter_spell||Actions||Counterspell oCounterSpellTarget.|
function|ActionEquipItem|nwn.action_equip_item|command|||action_equip_item||Actions||Equip oItem into nInventorySlot. - nInventorySlot: INVENTORY_SLOT_* * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionEquipItem failed." Note: If the creature already has an item equipped in the slot specified, it will be unequipped automatically by the call to ActionEquipItem. In order for ActionEquipItem to succeed the creature must be able to equip the item oItem normally. This means that: 1) The item is in the creature's inventory. 2) The item must already be identified (if magical). 3) The creature has the level required to equip the item (if magical and ILR is on). 4) The creature possesses the required feats to equip the item (such as weapon proficiencies).|
function|ActionEquipMostDamagingMelee|nwn.action_equip_most_damaging_melee|command||bOffHand:Bool|action_equip_most_damaging_melee||Actions||The creature will equip the melee weapon in its possession that can do the most damage. If no valid melee weapon is found, it will equip the most damaging range weapon. This function should only ever be called in the EndOfCombatRound scripts, because otherwise it would have to stop the combat round to run simulation. - oVersus: You can try to get the most damaging weapon against oVersus - bOffHand|
function|ActionEquipMostDamagingRanged|nwn.action_equip_most_damaging_ranged|command|||action_equip_most_damaging_ranged||Actions||The creature will equip the range weapon in its possession that can do the most damage. If no valid range weapon can be found, it will equip the most damaging melee weapon. - oVersus: You can try to get the most damaging weapon against oVersus|
function|ActionEquipMostEffectiveArmor|nwn.action_equip_most_effective_armor|command|||action_equip_most_effective_armor||Effects||The creature will equip the armour in its possession that has the highest armour class.|
function|ActionExamine|nwn.action_examine|command|||action_examine||Actions||Makes a player examine the object oExamine. This causes the examination pop-up box to appear for the object specified.|
function|ActionForceFollowObject|nwn.action_force_follow_object|command|||action_force_follow_object||Actions||The action subject will follow oFollow until a ClearAllActions() is called. - oFollow: this is the object to be followed - fFollowDistance: follow distance in metres * No return value|
function|ActionForceMoveToLocation|nwn.action_force_move_to_location|command||lDestination:Location,bRun:Bool|action_force_move_to_location||Actions||Force the action subject to move to lDestination.|
function|ActionForceMoveToObject|nwn.action_force_move_to_object|command||bRun:Bool|action_force_move_to_object||Actions||Force the action subject to move to oMoveTo.|
function|ActionGiveItem|nwn.action_give_item|command|||action_give_item||Actions||Give oItem to oGiveTo If oItem is not a valid item, or oGiveTo is not a valid object, nothing will happen.|
function|ActionInteractObject|nwn.action_interact_object|command|||action_interact_object||Actions||Use oPlaceable.|
function|ActionJumpToLocation|nwn.action_jump_to_location|command||lLocation:Location|action_jump_to_location||Actions||The subject will jump to lLocation instantly (even between areas). If lLocation is invalid, nothing will happen.|
function|ActionJumpToObject|nwn.action_jump_to_object|command||bWalkStraightLineToPoint:Bool|action_jump_to_object||Actions||Jump to an object ID, or as near to it as possible.|
function|ActionLockObject|nwn.action_lock_object|command|||action_lock_object||Actions||The action subject will lock oTarget, which can be a door or a placeable object.|
function|ActionMoveAwayFromLocation|nwn.action_move_away_from_location|command||lMoveAwayFrom:Location,bRun:Bool|action_move_away_from_location||Actions||Causes the action subject to move away from lMoveAwayFrom.|
function|ActionMoveAwayFromObject|nwn.action_move_away_from_object|command||bRun:Bool|action_move_away_from_object||Actions||Cause the action subject to move to a certain distance away from oFleeFrom. - oFleeFrom: This is the object we wish the action subject to move away from. If oFleeFrom is not in the same area as the action subject, nothing will happen. - bRun: If this is TRUE, the action subject will run rather than walk - fMoveAwayRange: This is the distance we wish the action subject to put between themselves and oFleeFrom * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionMoveAwayFromObject failed."|
function|ActionMoveToLocation|nwn.action_move_to_location|command||lDestination:Location,bRun:Bool|action_move_to_location||Actions||The action subject will move to lDestination. - lDestination: The object will move to this location. If the location is invalid or a path cannot be found to it, the command does nothing. - bRun: If this is TRUE, the action subject will run rather than walk * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "MoveToPoint failed."|
function|ActionMoveToObject|nwn.action_move_to_object|command||bRun:Bool|action_move_to_object||Actions||Cause the action subject to move to a certain distance from oMoveTo. If there is no path to oMoveTo, this command will do nothing. - oMoveTo: This is the object we wish the action subject to move to - bRun: If this is TRUE, the action subject will run rather than walk - fRange: This is the desired distance between the action subject and oMoveTo * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionMoveToObject failed."|
function|ActionOpenDoor|nwn.action_open_door|command||bRun:Bool|action_open_door||Actions||Cause the action subject to open oDoor - bRun: If TRUE, subject will run to the door instead of walking|
function|ActionPauseConversation|nwn.action_pause_conversation|command|||action_pause_conversation||Actions||Pause the current conversation.|
function|ActionPickUpItem|nwn.action_pick_up_item|command|||action_pick_up_item||Actions||Pick up oItem from the ground. * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionPickUpItem failed."|
function|ActionPlayAnimation|nwn.action_play_animation|command|||action_play_animation||Actions||Cause the action subject to play an animation - nAnimation: ANIMATION_* - fSpeed: Speed of the animation - fDurationSeconds: Duration of the animation (this is not used for Fire and Forget animations)|
function|ActionPutDownItem|nwn.action_put_down_item|command|||action_put_down_item||Actions||Put down oItem on the ground. * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionPutDownItem failed."|
function|ActionRandomWalk|nwn.action_random_walk|command|||action_random_walk||Actions||The action subject will generate a random location near its current location and pathfind to it. ActionRandomwalk never ends, which means it is neccessary to call ClearAllActions in order to allow a creature to perform any other action once ActionRandomWalk has been called. * No return value, but if an error occurs the log file will contain "ActionRandomWalk failed."|
function|ActionRest|nwn.action_rest|command||bCreatureToEnemyLineOfSightCheck:Bool|action_rest||Actions||The creature will rest if not in combat and no enemies are nearby. - bCreatureToEnemyLineOfSightCheck: TRUE to allow the creature to rest if enemies are nearby, but the creature can't see the enemy. FALSE the creature will not rest if enemies are nearby regardless of whether or not the creature can see them, such as if an enemy is close by, but is in a different room behind a closed door.|
function|ActionResumeConversation|nwn.action_resume_conversation|command|||action_resume_conversation||Actions||Resume a conversation after it has been paused.|
function|ActionSit|nwn.action_sit|command|||action_sit||Actions||Sit in oChair. Note: Not all creatures will be able to sit and not all objects can be sat on. The object oChair must also be marked as usable in the toolset. For Example: To get a player to sit in oChair when they click on it, place the following script in the OnUsed event for the object oChair. void main() { object oChair = OBJECT_SELF; AssignCommand(GetLastUsedBy(),ActionSit(oChair)); }|
function|ActionSpeakString|nwn.action_speak_string|command|||action_speak_string||Actions||Add a speak action to the action subject. - sStringToSpeak: String to be spoken - nTalkVolume: TALKVOLUME_*|
function|ActionSpeakStringByStrRef|nwn.action_speak_string_by_str_ref|command|||action_speak_string_by_str_ref||Actions||Causes the creature to speak a translated string. - nStrRef: Reference of the string in the talk table - nTalkVolume: TALKVOLUME_*|
function|ActionStartConversation|nwn.action_start_conversation|command||bPrivateConversation:Bool,bPlayHello:Bool|action_start_conversation||Actions||Starts a conversation with oObjectToConverseWith - this will cause their OnDialog event to fire. - oObjectToConverseWith - sDialogResRef: If this is blank, the creature's own dialogue file will be used - bPrivateConversation Turn off bPlayHello if you don't want the initial greeting to play|
function|ActionTakeItem|nwn.action_take_item|command|||action_take_item||Actions||Take oItem from oTakeFrom If oItem is not a valid item, or oTakeFrom is not a valid object, nothing will happen.|
function|ActionUnequipItem|nwn.action_unequip_item|command|||action_unequip_item||Actions||Unequip oItem from whatever slot it is currently in.|
function|ActionUnlockObject|nwn.action_unlock_object|command|||action_unlock_object||Actions||The action subject will unlock oTarget, which can be a door or a placeable object.|
function|ActionUseFeat|nwn.action_use_feat|command||lTarget:Location:target_location|action_use_feat||Actions||Use nFeat on oTarget. - nFeat: FEAT_* - oTarget: Target of the feat. Must be OBJECT_INVALID if lTarget is used. - nSubFeat: - For feats with subdial options, use either: - SUBFEAT_* for some specific feats like called shot - spells.2da line of the subdial spell, eg 708 for Dragon Shape: Blue Dragon when using FEAT_EPIC_WILD_SHAPE_DRAGON - lTarget: The location to use the feat at. oTarget must be OBJECT_INVALID for this to be used.|
function|ActionUseSkill|nwn.action_use_skill|command|||action_use_skill||Actions||Runs the action "UseSkill" on the current creature Use nSkill on oTarget. - nSkill: SKILL_* - oTarget - nSubSkill: SUBSKILL_* - oItemUsed: Item to use in conjunction with the skill|
function|ActionWait|nwn.action_wait|command|||action_wait||Actions||Do nothing for fSeconds seconds.|
function|AddHenchman|nwn.add_henchman|action|||add_henchman||Objects||Add oHenchman as a henchman to oMaster If oHenchman is either a DM or a player character, this will have no effect.|
function|AddJournalQuestEntry|nwn.add_journal_quest_entry|action||bAllPartyMembers:Bool,bAllPlayers:Bool,bAllowOverrideHigher:Bool|||Objects||Add a journal quest entry to oCreature. - szPlotID: the plot identifier used in the toolset's Journal Editor - nState: the state of the plot as seen in the toolset's Journal Editor - oCreature - bAllPartyMembers: If this is TRUE, the entry will show up in the journal of everyone in the party - bAllPlayers: If this is TRUE, the entry will show up in the journal of everyone in the world - bAllowOverrideHigher: If this is TRUE, you can set the state to a lower number than the one it is currently on|
function|AdjustAlignment|nwn.adjust_alignment|action||bAllPartyMembers:Bool|adjust_alignment||Creatures||Adjust the alignment of oSubject. - oSubject - nAlignment: -> ALIGNMENT_LAWFUL/ALIGNMENT_CHAOTIC/ALIGNMENT_GOOD/ALIGNMENT_EVIL: oSubject's alignment will be shifted in the direction specified -> ALIGNMENT_ALL: nShift will be added to oSubject's law/chaos and good/evil alignment values -> ALIGNMENT_NEUTRAL: nShift is applied to oSubject's law/chaos and good/evil alignment values in the direction which is towards neutrality. e.g. If oSubject has a law/chaos value of 10 (i.e. chaotic) and a good/evil value of 80 (i.e. good) then if nShift is 15, the law/chaos value will become (10+15)=25 and the good/evil value will become (80-25)=55 Furthermore, the shift will at most take the alignment value to 50 and not beyond. e.g. If oSubject has a law/chaos value of 40 and a good/evil value of 70, then if nShift is 15, the law/chaos value will become 50 and the good/evil value will become 55 - nShift: this is the desired shift in alignment - bAllPartyMembers: when TRUE the alignment shift of oSubject also has a diminished affect all members of oSubject's party (if oSubject is a Player). When FALSE the shift only affects oSubject. * No return value|
function|AdjustReputation|nwn.adjust_reputation|action|||adjust_reputation||Objects||Adjust how oSourceFactionMember's faction feels about oTarget by the specified amount. Note: This adjusts Faction Reputation, how the entire faction that oSourceFactionMember is in, feels about oTarget. * No return value Note: You can't adjust a player character's (PC) faction towards NPCs, so attempting to make an NPC hostile by passing in a PC object as oSourceFactionMember in the following call will fail: AdjustReputation(oNPC,oPC,-100); Instead you should pass in the PC object as the first parameter as in the following call which should succeed: AdjustReputation(oPC,oNPC,-100); Note: Will fail if oSourceFactionMember is a plot object.|
function|AmbientSoundChangeDay|nwn.ambient_sound_change_day|action|||ambient_sound_change_day||Areas and time||Change the ambient day track for oArea to nTrack. - oArea - nTrack|
function|AmbientSoundChangeNight|nwn.ambient_sound_change_night|action|||ambient_sound_change_night||Areas and time||Change the ambient night track for oArea to nTrack. - oArea - nTrack|
function|AmbientSoundPlay|nwn.ambient_sound_play|action|||ambient_sound_play||Areas and time||Play the ambient sound for oArea.|
function|AmbientSoundSetDayVolume|nwn.ambient_sound_set_day_volume|action|||ambient_sound_set_day_volume||Areas and time||Set the ambient day volume for oArea to nVolume. - oArea - nVolume: 0 - 100|
function|AmbientSoundSetNightVolume|nwn.ambient_sound_set_night_volume|action|||ambient_sound_set_night_volume||Areas and time||Set the ambient night volume for oArea to nVolume. - oArea - nVolume: 0 - 100|
function|AmbientSoundStop|nwn.ambient_sound_stop|action|||ambient_sound_stop||Areas and time||Stop the ambient sound for oArea.|
function|ApplyEffectAtLocation|nwn.apply_effect_at_location|action||eEffect:Effect,lLocation:Location|||Effects||Apply eEffect at lLocation.|
function|ApplyEffectToObject|nwn.apply_effect_to_object|manual|||||Effects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Nwn.ApplyEffectValueExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|BlackScreen|nwn.black_screen|action|||black_screen||Objects||Sets the screen to black. Can be used in preparation for a fade-in (FadeFromBlack) Can be cleared by either doing a FadeFromBlack, or by calling StopFade. - oCreature: creature controlled by player that should see black screen|
function|ChangeFaction|nwn.change_faction|action|||change_faction||Creatures||Make oObjectToChangeFaction join the faction of oMemberOfFactionToJoin. NB. ** This will only work for two NPCs **|
function|ChangeToStandardFaction|nwn.change_to_standard_faction|action|||change_to_standard_faction||Creatures||Make oCreatureToChange join one of the standard factions. ** This will only work on an NPC ** - nStandardFaction: STANDARD_FACTION_*|
function|ClearAllActions|nwn.clear_all_actions|command|||clear_actions||Actions||Clear all the actions of oObject. * No return value, but if an error occurs, the log file will contain "ClearAllActions failed.". - nClearCombatState: if true, this will immediately clear the combat state on a creature, which will stop the combat music and allow them to rest, engage in dialog, or other actions that they would normally have to wait for.|
function|CopyArea|nwn.copy_area|action|||copy_area||Areas and time||Creates a copy of a existing area, including everything inside of it (except players). Will optionally set a new area tag and displayed name. The new area is accessible immediately, but initialisation scripts for the area and all contained creatures will only run after the current script finishes (so you can clean up objects before returning). This is similar to CreateArea, except this variant will copy all changes made to the source area since it has spawned. CreateArea() will instance the area from the .are and .git data as it was at creation. Returns the new area, or OBJECT_INVALID on error. Note: You will have to manually adjust all transitions (doors, triggers) with the relevant script commands, or players might end up in the wrong area. Note: Areas cannot have duplicate ResRefs, so your new area will have a autogenerated, sequential resref starting with "nw_"; for example: nw_5. You cannot influence this resref. If you destroy an area, that resref will be come free for reuse for the next area created. If you need to know the resref of your new area, you can call GetResRef on it.|
function|CopyItem|nwn.copy_item|action||bCopyVars:Bool|copy_item||Items||duplicates the item and returns a new object oItem - item to copy oTargetInventory - create item in this object's inventory. If this parameter is not valid, the item will be created in oItem's location bCopyVars - copy the local variables from the old item to the new one * returns the new item * returns OBJECT_INVALID for non-items. * can only copy empty item containers. will return OBJECT_INVALID if oItem contains other items. * if it is possible to merge this item with any others in the target location, then it will do so and return the merged object.|
function|CopyItemAndModify|nwn.copy_item_and_modify|action||bCopyVars:Bool|copy_item_and_modify||Items||Creates a new copy of an item, while making a single change to the appearance of the item. Helmet models and simple items ignore iIndex. iType iIndex iNewValue ITEM_APPR_TYPE_SIMPLE_MODEL [Ignored] Model # ITEM_APPR_TYPE_WEAPON_COLOR ITEM_APPR_WEAPON_COLOR_* 1-4 ITEM_APPR_TYPE_WEAPON_MODEL ITEM_APPR_WEAPON_MODEL_* Model # ITEM_APPR_TYPE_ARMOR_MODEL ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_MODEL_* Model # ITEM_APPR_TYPE_ARMOR_COLOR ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_COLOR_* [0] 0-175 [1] [0] Alternatively, where ITEM_APPR_TYPE_ARMOR_COLOR is specified, if per-part coloring is desired, the following equation can be used for nIndex to achieve that: ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_NUM_COLORS + (ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_MODEL_ * ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_NUM_COLORS) + ITEM_APPR_ARMOR_COLOR_ For example, to change the CLOTH1 channel of the torso, nIndex would be: 6 + (7 * 6) + 2 = 50 [1] When specifying per-part coloring, the value 255 is allowed and corresponds with the logical function 'clear colour override', which clears the per-part override for that part.|
function|CopyObject|nwn.copy_object|action||locLocation:Location,bCopyLocalState:Bool|copy_object||Objects||Duplicates the object specified by oSource. NOTE: this command can be used for copying Creatures, Items, Placeables, Waypoints, Stores, Doors, Triggers, Encounters. If an owner is specified and the object is an item, it will be put into their inventory Otherwise, it will be created at the location. If a new tag is specified, it will be assigned to the new object. If bCopyLocalState is TRUE, local vars, effects, action queue, and transition info (triggers, doors) are copied over.|
function|CreateArea|nwn.create_area|action|||||Areas and time||Instances a new area from the given sSourceResRef, which needs to be a existing module area. Will optionally set a new area tag and displayed name. The new area is accessible immediately, but initialisation scripts for the area and all contained creatures will only run after the current script finishes (so you can clean up objects before returning). Returns the new area, or OBJECT_INVALID on failure. Note: When spawning a second instance of a existing area, you will have to manually adjust all transitions (doors, triggers) with the relevant script commands, or players might end up in the wrong area. Note: Areas cannot have duplicate ResRefs, so your new area will have a autogenerated, sequential resref starting with "nw_"; for example: nw_5. You cannot influence this resref. If you destroy an area, that resref will be come free for reuse for the next area created. If you need to know the resref of your new area, you can call GetResRef on it. Note: When instancing an area from a loaded savegame, it will spawn the area as it was at time of save, NOT at module creation. This is because the savegame replaces the module data. Due to technical limitations, polymorphed creatures, personal reputation, and associates will currently fail to restore correctly.|
function|CreateItemOnObject|nwn.create_item_on_object|action|||||Items||Create an item with the template sItemTemplate in oTarget's inventory. - nStackSize: This is the stack size of the item to be created - sNewTag: If this string is not empty, it will replace the default tag from the template * Return value: The object that has been created. On error, this returns OBJECT_INVALID. If the item created was merged into an existing stack of similar items, the function will return the merged stack object. If the merged stack overflowed, the function will return the overflowed stack that was created.|
function|CreateObject|nwn.create_object|action||lLocation:Location,bUseAppearAnimation:Bool|||Objects||Create an object of the specified type at lLocation. - nObjectType: OBJECT_TYPE_ITEM, OBJECT_TYPE_CREATURE, OBJECT_TYPE_PLACEABLE, OBJECT_TYPE_STORE, OBJECT_TYPE_WAYPOINT - sTemplate - lLocation - bUseAppearAnimation - sNewTag - if this string is not empty, it will replace the default tag from the template|
function|CreateTrapAtLocation|nwn.create_trap_at_location|action||lLocation:Location|||Objects||Creates a square Trap object. - nTrapType: The base type of trap (TRAP_BASE_TYPE_*) - lLocation: The location and orientation that the trap will be created at. - fSize: The size of the trap. Minimum size allowed is 1.0f. - sTag: The tag of the trap being created. - nFaction: The faction of the trap (STANDARD_FACTION_*). - sOnDisarmScript: The OnDisarm script that will fire when the trap is disarmed. If "" no script will fire. - sOnTrapTriggeredScript: The OnTrapTriggered script that will fire when the trap is triggered. If "" the default OnTrapTriggered script for the trap type specified will fire instead (as specified in the traps.2da).|
function|CreateTrapOnObject|nwn.create_trap_on_object|action|||||Objects||Creates a Trap on the object specified. - nTrapType: The base type of trap (TRAP_BASE_TYPE_*) - oObject: The object that the trap will be created on. Works only on Doors and Placeables. - nFaction: The faction of the trap (STANDARD_FACTION_*). - sOnDisarmScript: The OnDisarm script that will fire when the trap is disarmed. If "" no script will fire. - sOnTrapTriggeredScript: The OnTrapTriggered script that will fire when the trap is triggered. If "" the default OnTrapTriggered script for the trap type specified will fire instead (as specified in the traps.2da). Note: After creating a trap on an object, you can change the trap's properties using the various SetTrap* scripting commands by passing in the object that the trap was created on (i.e. oObject) to any subsequent SetTrap* commands.|
function|DeleteLocalFloat|nwn.delete_local_float|action|||delete_local_float||Locals||Delete oObject's local float variable sVarName|
function|DeleteLocalInt|nwn.delete_local_int|action|||delete_local_int||Locals||Delete oObject's local integer variable sVarName|
function|DeleteLocalLocation|nwn.delete_local_location|action|||delete_local_location||Locals||Delete oObject's local location variable sVarName|
function|DeleteLocalObject|nwn.delete_local_object|action|||delete_local_object||Locals||Delete oObject's local object variable sVarName|
function|DeleteLocalString|nwn.delete_local_string|action|||delete_local_string||Locals||Delete oObject's local string variable sVarName|
function|DestroyArea|nwn.destroy_area|action|||destroy_area||Areas and time||Destroys the given area object and everything in it. If the area is in a module, the .are and .git data is left behind and you can spawn from it again. If the area is a temporary copy, the data will be deleted and you cannot spawn it again via the resref. Return values: 0: Object not an area or invalid. -1: Area contains spawn location and removal would leave module without entrypoint. -2: Players in area. 1: Area destroyed successfully.|
function|DestroyObject|nwn.destroy_object|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Actions.DespawnCreatureExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|DoDoorAction|nwn.do_door_action|action|||do_door_action||Objects||Perform nDoorAction on oTargetDoor.|
function|DoPlaceableObjectAction|nwn.do_placeable_object_action|action|||do_placeable_object_action||Objects||The caller performs nPlaceableAction on oPlaceable. - oPlaceable - nPlaceableAction: PLACEABLE_ACTION_*|
function|EffectACDecrease|nwn.effect_ac_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.ac_decrease|Effects||Create an AC Decrease effect. - nValue - nModifyType: AC_* - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* * Default value for nDamageType should only ever be used in this function prototype.|
function|EffectACIncrease|nwn.effect_ac_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.ac_increase|Effects||Create an AC Increase effect - nValue: size of AC increase - nModifyType: AC_*_BONUS - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* * Default value for nDamageType should only ever be used in this function prototype.|
function|EffectAbilityDecrease|nwn.effect_ability_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.ability_decrease|Effects||Create an Ability Decrease effect. - nAbility: ABILITY_* - nModifyBy: This is the amount by which to decrement the ability|
function|EffectAbilityIncrease|nwn.effect_ability_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.ability_increase|Effects||Create an Ability Increase effect - bAbilityToIncrease: ABILITY_*|
function|EffectAppear|nwn.effect_appear|pure|Effect|||effect.appear|Effects||Create an Appear effect to make the object "fly in". - nAnimation determines which appear and disappear animations to use. Most creatures only have animation 1, although a few have 2 (like beholders)|
function|EffectAttackDecrease|nwn.effect_attack_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.attack_decrease|Effects||Create an Attack Decrease effect. - nPenalty - nModifierType: ATTACK_BONUS_*|
function|EffectAttackIncrease|nwn.effect_attack_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.attack_increase|Effects||Create an Attack Increase effect - nBonus: size of attack bonus - nModifierType: ATTACK_BONUS_*|
function|EffectBeam|nwn.effect_beam|pure|Effect|bMissEffect:Bool,vTranslate:omit,vRotate:omit||effect.beam|Effects||Create a Beam effect. - nBeamVisualEffect: VFX_BEAM_* - oEffector: the beam is emitted from this creature - nBodyPart: BODY_NODE_* - bMissEffect: If this is TRUE, the beam will fire to a random vector near or past the target * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nBeamVisualEffect is not valid.|
function|EffectBlindness|nwn.effect_blindness|pure|Effect|||effect.blindness|Effects||Create a Blindness effect.|
function|EffectBonusFeat|nwn.effect_bonus_feat|pure|Effect|||effect.bonus_feat|Effects||Creates a bonus feat effect. These act like the Bonus Feat item property, and do not work as feat prerequisites for levelup purposes. - nFeat: FEAT_*|
function|EffectCharmed|nwn.effect_charmed|pure|Effect|||effect.charmed|Effects||Create a Charm effect|
function|EffectConcealment|nwn.effect_concealment|pure|Effect|||effect.concealment|Effects||Create a Concealment effect. - nPercentage: 1-100 inclusive - nMissChanceType: MISS_CHANCE_TYPE_* * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nPercentage < 1 or nPercentage > 100.|
function|EffectConfused|nwn.effect_confused|pure|Effect|||effect.confused|Effects||Create a Confuse effect|
function|EffectCurse|nwn.effect_curse|pure|Effect|||effect.curse|Effects||Create a Curse effect. - nStrMod: strength modifier - nDexMod: dexterity modifier - nConMod: constitution modifier - nIntMod: intelligence modifier - nWisMod: wisdom modifier - nChaMod: charisma modifier|
function|EffectCutsceneDominated|nwn.effect_cutscene_dominated|pure|Effect|||effect.cutscene_dominated|Effects||Returns an effect that is guaranteed to dominate a creature Like EffectDominated but cannot be resisted|
function|EffectCutsceneGhost|nwn.effect_cutscene_ghost|pure|Effect|||effect.cutscene_ghost|Effects||Creates a cutscene ghost effect, this will allow creatures to pathfind through other creatures without bumping into them for the duration of the effect.|
function|EffectCutsceneImmobilize|nwn.effect_cutscene_immobilize|pure|Effect|||effect.cutscene_immobilize|Effects||Returns an effect that when applied will paralyze the target's legs, rendering them unable to walk but otherwise unpenalized. This effect cannot be resisted.|
function|EffectCutsceneParalyze|nwn.effect_cutscene_paralyze|pure|Effect|||effect.cutscene_paralyze|Effects||returns an effect that is guaranteed to paralyze a creature. this effect is identical to EffectParalyze except that it cannot be resisted.|
function|EffectDamage|nwn.effect_damage|pure|Effect|||effect.damage|Effects||Create a Damage effect - nDamageAmount: amount of damage to be dealt. This should be applied as an instantaneous effect. - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* - nDamagePower: DAMAGE_POWER_*|
function|EffectDamageDecrease|nwn.effect_damage_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.damage_decrease|Effects||Create a Damage Decrease effect. - nPenalty - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_*|
function|EffectDamageImmunityDecrease|nwn.effect_damage_immunity_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.damage_immunity_decrease|Effects||Create a Damage Immunity Decrease effect. - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* - nPercentImmunity|
function|EffectDamageImmunityIncrease|nwn.effect_damage_immunity_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.damage_immunity_increase|Effects||Creates a Damage Immunity Increase effect. - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* - nPercentImmunity|
function|EffectDamageIncrease|nwn.effect_damage_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.damage_increase|Effects||Create a Damage Increase effect - nBonus: DAMAGE_BONUS_* - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* NOTE! You *must* use the DAMAGE_BONUS_* constants! Using other values may result in odd behaviour.|
function|EffectDamageReduction|nwn.effect_damage_reduction|pure|Effect|bRangedOnly:Bool||effect.damage_reduction|Effects||Create a Damage Reduction effect - nAmount: amount of damage reduction - nDamagePower: DAMAGE_POWER_* - nLimit: How much damage the effect can absorb before disappearing. Set to zero for infinite - bRangedOnly: Set to TRUE to have this reduction only apply to ranged attacks|
function|EffectDamageResistance|nwn.effect_damage_resistance|pure|Effect|bRangedOnly:Bool||effect.damage_resistance|Effects||Create a Damage Resistance effect that removes the first nAmount points of damage of type nDamageType, up to nLimit (or infinite if nLimit is 0) - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* - nAmount: The amount of damage to soak each time the target is damaged. - nLimit: How much damage the effect can absorb before disappearing. Set to zero for infinite. - bRangedOnly: Set to TRUE to have this resistance only apply to ranged attacks.|
function|EffectDamageShield|nwn.effect_damage_shield|pure|Effect|||effect.damage_shield|Effects||Create a Damage Shield effect which does (nDamageAmount + nRandomAmount) damage to any melee attacker on a successful attack of damage type nDamageType. - nDamageAmount: an integer value - nRandomAmount: DAMAGE_BONUS_* - nDamageType: DAMAGE_TYPE_* NOTE! You *must* use the DAMAGE_BONUS_* constants! Using other values may result in odd behaviour.|
function|EffectDarkness|nwn.effect_darkness|pure|Effect|||effect.darkness|Effects||Create a Darkness effect.|
function|EffectDazed|nwn.effect_dazed|pure|Effect|||effect.dazed|Effects||Create a Daze effect|
function|EffectDeaf|nwn.effect_deaf|pure|Effect|||effect.deaf|Effects||Create a Deaf effect|
function|EffectDeath|nwn.effect_death|pure|Effect|||effect.death|Effects||Create a Death effect - nSpectacularDeath: if this is TRUE, the creature to which this effect is applied will die in an extraordinary fashion - nDisplayFeedback|
function|EffectDisappear|nwn.effect_disappear|pure|Effect|||effect.disappear|Effects||Create a Disappear effect to make the object "fly away" and then destroy itself. - nAnimation determines which appear and disappear animations to use. Most creatures only have animation 1, although a few have 2 (like beholders)|
function|EffectDisappearAppear|nwn.effect_disappear_appear|pure|Effect|lLocation:Location||effect.disappear_appear|Effects||Create a Disappear/Appear effect. The object will "fly away" for the duration of the effect and will reappear at lLocation. - nAnimation determines which appear and disappear animations to use. Most creatures only have animation 1, although a few have 2 (like beholders)|
function|EffectDisease|nwn.effect_disease|pure|Effect|||effect.disease|Effects||Create a Disease effect. - nDiseaseType: DISEASE_*|
function|EffectDispelMagicAll|nwn.effect_dispel_magic_all|pure|Effect|||effect.dispel_magic_all|Effects||Create a Dispel Magic All effect. If no parameter is specified, USE_CREATURE_LEVEL will be used. This will cause the dispel effect to use the level of the creature that created the effect.|
function|EffectDispelMagicBest|nwn.effect_dispel_magic_best|pure|Effect|||effect.dispel_magic_best|Effects||Create a Dispel Magic Best effect. If no parameter is specified, USE_CREATURE_LEVEL will be used. This will cause the dispel effect to use the level of the creature that created the effect.|
function|EffectDominated|nwn.effect_dominated|pure|Effect|||effect.dominated|Effects||Create a Dominate effect|
function|EffectEnemyAttackBonus|nwn.effect_enemy_attack_bonus|pure|Effect|||effect.enemy_attack_bonus|Effects||Create an Enemy Attack Bonus effect. Creatures attacking the given creature with melee/ranged attacks or touch attacks get a bonus to hit.|
function|EffectEntangle|nwn.effect_entangle|pure|Effect|||effect.entangle|Effects||Create an Entangle effect When applied, this effect will restrict the creature's movement and apply a (-2) to all attacks and a -4 to AC.|
function|EffectEthereal|nwn.effect_ethereal|pure|Effect|||effect.ethereal|Effects||Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_ETHEREAL which works just like EffectSanctuary except that the observers get no saving throw|
function|EffectForceWalk|nwn.effect_force_walk|pure|Effect|||effect.force_walk|Effects||Forces the creature to always walk|
function|EffectFrightened|nwn.effect_frightened|pure|Effect|||effect.frightened|Effects||Create a Frighten effect|
function|EffectHaste|nwn.effect_haste|pure|Effect|||effect.haste|Effects||Create a Haste effect.|
function|EffectHeal|nwn.effect_heal|pure|Effect|||effect.heal|Effects||Create a Heal effect. This should be applied as an instantaneous effect. * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nDamageToHeal < 0.|
function|EffectHitPointChangeWhenDying|nwn.effect_hit_point_change_when_dying|pure|Effect|||effect.hit_point_change_when_dying|Effects||Create a Hit Point Change When Dying effect. - fHitPointChangePerRound: this can be positive or negative, but not zero. * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if fHitPointChangePerRound is 0.|
function|EffectIcon|nwn.effect_icon|pure|Effect|||effect.icon|Effects||Create an Icon effect. * nIconID: The effect icon (EFFECT_ICON_*) to display. Using the icon for Poison/Disease will also color the health bar green/brown, useful to simulate custom poisons/diseases. Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT when nIconID is < 1 or > 255.|
function|EffectImmunity|nwn.effect_immunity|pure|Effect|||effect.immunity|Effects||Create an Immunity effect. - nImmunityType: IMMUNITY_TYPE_*|
function|EffectInvisibility|nwn.effect_invisibility|pure|Effect|||effect.invisibility|Effects||Create an Invisibility effect. - nInvisibilityType: INVISIBILITY_TYPE_* * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nInvisibilityType is invalid.|
function|EffectKnockdown|nwn.effect_knockdown|pure|Effect|||effect.knockdown|Effects||Create a Knockdown effect This effect knocks creatures off their feet, they will sit until the effect is removed. This should be applied as a temporary effect with a 3 second duration minimum (1 second to fall, 1 second sitting, 1 second to get up).|
function|EffectLinkEffects|nwn.effect_link_effects|pure|Effect|eChildEffect:Effect,eParentEffect:Effect||effect.link_effects|Effects||Link the two supplied effects, returning eChildEffect as a child of eParentEffect. Note: When applying linked effects if the target is immune to all valid effects all other effects will be removed as well. This means that if you apply a visual effect and a silence effect (in a link) and the target is immune to the silence effect that the visual effect will get removed as well. Visual Effects are not considered "valid" effects for the purposes of determining if an effect will be removed or not and as such should never be packaged *only* with other visual effects in a link.|
function|EffectMissChance|nwn.effect_miss_chance|pure|Effect|||effect.miss_chance|Effects||Create a Miss Chance effect. - nPercentage: 1-100 inclusive - nMissChanceType: MISS_CHANCE_TYPE_* * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nPercentage < 1 or nPercentage > 100.|
function|EffectModifyAttacks|nwn.effect_modify_attacks|pure|Effect|||effect.modify_attacks|Effects||Create a Modify Attacks effect to add attacks. - nAttacks: maximum is 5, even with the effect stacked * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nAttacks > 5.|
function|EffectMovementSpeedDecrease|nwn.effect_movement_speed_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.movement_speed_decrease|Effects||Create a Movement Speed Decrease effect. - nPercentChange - range 0 through 99 eg. 0 = no change in speed 50 = 50% slower 99 = almost immobile|
function|EffectMovementSpeedIncrease|nwn.effect_movement_speed_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.movement_speed_increase|Effects||Create a Movement Speed Increase effect. - nPercentChange - range 0 through 99 eg. 0 = no change in speed 50 = 50% faster 99 = almost twice as fast|
function|EffectNegativeLevel|nwn.effect_negative_level|pure|Effect|bHPBonus:Bool||effect.negative_level|Effects||Create a Negative Level effect. - nNumLevels: the number of negative levels to apply. * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nNumLevels > 100.|
function|EffectPacified|nwn.effect_pacified|pure|Effect|||effect.pacified|Effects||Create a Pacified effect, making the creature unable to attack anyone|
function|EffectParalyze|nwn.effect_paralyze|pure|Effect|||effect.paralyze|Effects||Create a Paralyze effect|
function|EffectPetrify|nwn.effect_petrify|pure|Effect|||effect.petrify|Effects||returns an effect that will petrify the target * currently applies EffectParalyze and the stoneskin visual effect.|
function|EffectPoison|nwn.effect_poison|pure|Effect|||effect.poison|Effects||Create a Poison effect. - nPoisonType: POISON_*|
function|EffectPolymorph|nwn.effect_polymorph|pure|Effect|||effect.polymorph|Effects||Create a Polymorph effect. - nLocked: If TRUE the creature cannot cancel the polymorph. - nUnpolymorphVFX: If -1 no VFX will play when this polymorph is removed. Else will play the relevant VFX. - nSpellAbilityModifier: Set a custom spell ability modifier for the 3 polymorph spells. Save DC is 10 + Innate spell level + this ability modifier. -1 uses the creators spellcasting/feat using class spellcasting ability modifier. - nSpellAbilityCasterLevel: Set a custom caster level for the 3 polymorph spells. Default (0) is to use the first class slot class level as previously.|
function|EffectRegenerate|nwn.effect_regenerate|pure|Effect|||effect.regenerate|Effects||Create a Regenerate effect. - nAmount: amount of damage to be regenerated per time interval - fIntervalSeconds: length of interval in seconds|
function|EffectResurrection|nwn.effect_resurrection|pure|Effect|||effect.resurrection|Effects||Create a Resurrection effect. This should be applied as an instantaneous effect.|
function|EffectSanctuary|nwn.effect_sanctuary|pure|Effect|||effect.sanctuary|Effects||Create a Sanctuary effect. - nDifficultyClass: must be a non-zero, positive number * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nDifficultyClass <= 0.|
function|EffectSavingThrowDecrease|nwn.effect_saving_throw_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.saving_throw_decrease|Effects||Create a Saving Throw Decrease effect. - nSave: SAVING_THROW_* (not SAVING_THROW_TYPE_*) SAVING_THROW_ALL SAVING_THROW_FORT SAVING_THROW_REFLEX SAVING_THROW_WILL - nValue: size of the Saving Throw decrease - nSaveType: SAVING_THROW_TYPE_* (e.g. SAVING_THROW_TYPE_ACID )|
function|EffectSavingThrowIncrease|nwn.effect_saving_throw_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.saving_throw_increase|Effects||Create a Saving Throw Increase effect - nSave: SAVING_THROW_* (not SAVING_THROW_TYPE_*) SAVING_THROW_ALL SAVING_THROW_FORT SAVING_THROW_REFLEX SAVING_THROW_WILL - nValue: size of the Saving Throw increase - nSaveType: SAVING_THROW_TYPE_* (e.g. SAVING_THROW_TYPE_ACID )|
function|EffectSeeInvisible|nwn.effect_see_invisible|pure|Effect|||effect.see_invisible|Effects||Create a See Invisible effect.|
function|EffectSilence|nwn.effect_silence|pure|Effect|||effect.silence|Effects||Create a Silence effect.|
function|EffectSkillDecrease|nwn.effect_skill_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.skill_decrease|Effects||Create a Skill Decrease effect. * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nSkill is invalid.|
function|EffectSkillIncrease|nwn.effect_skill_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.skill_increase|Effects||Create a Skill Increase effect. - nSkill: SKILL_* - nValue * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nSkill is invalid.|
function|EffectSleep|nwn.effect_sleep|pure|Effect|||effect.sleep|Effects||Create a Sleep effect|
function|EffectSlow|nwn.effect_slow|pure|Effect|||effect.slow|Effects||Create a Slow effect.|
function|EffectSpellFailure|nwn.effect_spell_failure|pure|Effect|||effect.spell_failure|Effects||Creates an effect that inhibits spells - nPercent - percentage of failure - nSpellSchool - the school of spells affected. Only applies to SPELL_FAILURE_TYPE_ALL. - nSpellFailureType - Use SPELL_FAILURE_TYPE_* constants for different spell failure types|
function|EffectSpellImmunity|nwn.effect_spell_immunity|pure|Effect|||effect.spell_immunity|Effects||Create a Spell Immunity effect. There is a known bug with this function. There *must* be a parameter specified when this is called (even if the desired parameter is SPELL_ALL_SPELLS), otherwise an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT will be returned. - nImmunityToSpell: SPELL_* * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nImmunityToSpell is invalid.|
function|EffectSpellLevelAbsorption|nwn.effect_spell_level_absorption|pure|Effect|||effect.spell_level_absorption|Effects||Create a Spell Level Absorption effect. - nMaxSpellLevelAbsorbed: maximum spell level that will be absorbed by the effect - nTotalSpellLevelsAbsorbed: maximum number of spell levels that will be absorbed by the effect - nSpellSchool: SPELL_SCHOOL_* * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if: nMaxSpellLevelAbsorbed is not between -1 and 9 inclusive, or nSpellSchool is invalid.|
function|EffectSpellResistanceDecrease|nwn.effect_spell_resistance_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.spell_resistance_decrease|Effects||Create a Spell Resistance Decrease effect.|
function|EffectSpellResistanceIncrease|nwn.effect_spell_resistance_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.spell_resistance_increase|Effects||Create a Spell Resistance Increase effect. - nValue: size of spell resistance increase|
function|EffectStunned|nwn.effect_stunned|pure|Effect|||effect.stunned|Effects||Create a Stun effect|
function|EffectSummonCreature|nwn.effect_summon_creature|pure|Effect|||effect.summon_creature|Effects||Create a Summon Creature effect. The creature is created and placed into the caller's party/faction. - sCreatureResref: Identifies the creature to be summoned - nVisualEffectId: VFX_* - fDelaySeconds: There can be delay between the visual effect being played, and the creature being added to the area - nUseAppearAnimation: should this creature play it's "appear" animation when it is summoned. If zero, it will just fade in somewhere near the target. If the value is 1 it will use the appear animation, and if it's 2 it will use appear2 (which doesn't exist for most creatures) - nUnsummonVisualEffectId: VFX_* to apply when the creature is unsummoned - oSummonToAdd: If sCreatureResref is blank, this object (if they have no master) is instead added as the summon, applying nVisualEffectId at their location fDelaySeconds and nUseAppearAnimation are unused, and no "Summoned a creature" feedback is sent, allowing you to do your own. The creature otherwise acts like a summon from then on, including not giving out XP for being killed, and able to be unsummoned by the master or when the effect expires.|
function|EffectSwarm|nwn.effect_swarm|pure|Effect|||effect.swarm|Effects||Create a Swarm effect. - nLooping: If this is TRUE, for the duration of the effect when one creature created by this effect dies, the next one in the list will be created. If the last creature in the list dies, we loop back to the beginning and sCreatureTemplate1 will be created, and so on... - sCreatureTemplate1 - sCreatureTemplate2 - sCreatureTemplate3 - sCreatureTemplate4|
function|EffectTemporaryHitpoints|nwn.effect_temporary_hitpoints|pure|Effect|||effect.temporary_hitpoints|Effects||Create a Temporary Hitpoints effect. - nHitPoints: a positive integer * Returns an effect of type EFFECT_TYPE_INVALIDEFFECT if nHitPoints < 0.|
function|EffectTimeStop|nwn.effect_time_stop|pure|Effect|||effect.time_stop|Effects||Create a Time Stop effect.|
function|EffectTimeStopImmunity|nwn.effect_time_stop_immunity|pure|Effect|||effect.time_stop_immunity|Effects||Provides immunity to the effects of EffectTimeStop which allows actions during other creatures time stop effects|
function|EffectTrueSeeing|nwn.effect_true_seeing|pure|Effect|||effect.true_seeing|Effects||Create a True Seeing effect.|
function|EffectTurnResistanceDecrease|nwn.effect_turn_resistance_decrease|pure|Effect|||effect.turn_resistance_decrease|Effects||Create a Turn Resistance Decrease effect. - nHitDice: a positive number representing the number of hit dice for the / decrease|
function|EffectTurnResistanceIncrease|nwn.effect_turn_resistance_increase|pure|Effect|||effect.turn_resistance_increase|Effects||Create a Turn Resistance Increase effect. - nHitDice: a positive number representing the number of hit dice for the increase|
function|EffectTurned|nwn.effect_turned|pure|Effect|||effect.turned|Effects||Create a Turned effect. Turned effects are supernatural by default.|
function|EffectUltravision|nwn.effect_ultravision|pure|Effect|||effect.ultravision|Effects||Create an Ultravision effect.|
function|EffectVisualEffect|nwn.effect_visual_effect|pure|Effect|vTranslate:omit,vRotate:omit||effect.visual_effect|Effects||* Create a Visual Effect that can be applied to an object. - nVisualEffectId - nMissEffect: if this is TRUE, a random vector near or past the target will be generated, on which to play the effect|
function|ExploreAreaForPlayer|nwn.explore_area_for_player|action||bExplored:Bool|explore_area_for_player||Areas and time||Expose/Hide the entire map of oArea for oPlayer. - oArea: The area that the map will be exposed/hidden for. - oPlayer: The player the map will be exposed/hidden for. - bExplored: TRUE/FALSE. Whether the map should be completely explored or hidden.|
function|ExtraordinaryEffect|nwn.extraordinary_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|extraordinary_effect||Effects||Set the subtype of eEffect to Extraordinary and return eEffect. (Effects default to magical if the subtype is not set) Extraordinary effects are removed by resting, but not by dispel magic|
function|FadeFromBlack|nwn.fade_from_black|action|||fade_from_black||Objects||Fades the screen for the given creature/player from black to regular screen - oCreature: creature controlled by player that should fade from black|
function|FadeToBlack|nwn.fade_to_black|action|||fade_to_black||Objects||Fades the screen for the given creature/player from regular screen to black - oCreature: creature controlled by player that should fade to black|
function|FloatingTextStrRefOnCreature|nwn.floating_text_str_ref_on_creature|action||bBroadcastToFaction:Bool,bChatWindow:Bool|||Creatures||Display floaty text above the specified creature. The text will also appear in the chat buffer of each player that receives the floaty text. - nStrRefToDisplay: String ref (therefore text is translated) - oCreatureToFloatAbove - bBroadcastToFaction: If this is TRUE then only creatures in the same faction as oCreatureToFloatAbove will see the floaty text, and only if they are within range (30 metres). - bChatWindow: If TRUE, the string reference will be displayed in oCreatureToFloatAbove's chat window|
function|FloatingTextStringOnCreature|nwn.floating_text_string_on_creature|action||bBroadcastToFaction:Bool,bChatWindow:Bool|||Creatures||Display floaty text above the specified creature. The text will also appear in the chat buffer of each player that receives the floaty text. - sStringToDisplay: String - oCreatureToFloatAbove - bBroadcastToFaction: If this is TRUE then only creatures in the same faction as oCreatureToFloatAbove will see the floaty text, and only if they are within range (30 metres). - bChatWindow: If TRUE, sStringToDisplay will be displayed in oCreatureToFloatAbove's chat window.|
function|ForceRest|nwn.force_rest|action|||force_rest||Objects||Instantly gives this creature the benefits of a rest (restored hitpoints, spells, feats, etc..)|
function|GetAC|nwn.get_ac|manual|||||Creatures|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetCreatureACExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetAILevel|nwn.get_ai_level|pure|||get_ai_level||Objects||Gets the current AI Level that the creature is running at. Returns one of the following: AI_LEVEL_INVALID, AI_LEVEL_VERY_LOW, AI_LEVEL_LOW, AI_LEVEL_NORMAL, AI_LEVEL_HIGH, AI_LEVEL_VERY_HIGH|
function|GetAbilityModifier|nwn.get_ability_modifier|pure|||||Creatures||Returns the ability modifier for the specified ability Get oCreature's ability modifier for nAbility. - nAbility: ABILITY_* - oCreature|
function|GetAbilityScore|nwn.get_ability_score|pure||nBaseAbilityScore:Bool|get_ability_score||Creatures||Get the ability score of type nAbility for a creature (otherwise 0) - oCreature: the creature whose ability score we wish to find out - nAbilityType: ABILITY_* - nBaseAbilityScore: if set to true will return the base ability score without bonuses (e.g. ability bonuses granted from equipped items). Return value on error: 0|
function|GetActionMode|nwn.get_action_mode|pure|||get_action_mode||Objects||Gets the status of ACTION_MODE_* modes on a creature.|
function|GetAge|nwn.get_age|pure|||get_age||Objects||Get oCreature's age. * Returns 0 if oCreature is invalid.|
function|GetAlignmentGoodEvil|nwn.get_alignment_good_evil|pure|||get_alignment_good_evil||Creatures||Return an ALIGNMENT_* constant to represent oCreature's good/evil alignment * Return value if oCreature is not a valid creature: -1|
function|GetAlignmentLawChaos|nwn.get_alignment_law_chaos|pure|||get_alignment_law_chaos||Creatures||Return an ALIGNMENT_* constant to represent oCreature's law/chaos alignment * Return value if oCreature is not a valid creature: -1|
function|GetAnimalCompanionCreatureType|nwn.get_animal_companion_creature_type|pure|||get_animal_companion_creature_type||Creatures||Get oCreature's animal companion creature type (ANIMAL_COMPANION_CREATURE_TYPE_*). * Returns ANIMAL_COMPANION_CREATURE_TYPE_NONE if oCreature is invalid or does not currently have an animal companion.|
function|GetAnimalCompanionName|nwn.get_animal_companion_name|pure|||get_animal_companion_name||Objects||Get oCreature's animal companion's name. * Returns "" if oCreature is invalid, does not currently have an animal companion or if the animal companion's name is blank.|
function|GetAppearanceType|nwn.get_appearance_type|pure|||get_appearance_type||Objects||returns the appearance type of the specified creature. * returns a constant APPEARANCE_TYPE_* for valid creatures * returns APPEARANCE_TYPE_INVALID for non creatures/invalid creatures|
function|GetArcaneSpellFailure|nwn.get_arcane_spell_failure|pure|||get_arcane_spell_failure||Creatures||Returns the current arcane spell failure factor of a creature|
function|GetArea|nwn.get_area|pure|||get_area||Areas and time||Get the area that oTarget is currently in * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetAreaFromLocation|nwn.get_area_from_location|pure||lLocation:Location|get_area||Areas and time||Get the area's object ID from lLocation.|
function|GetAreaLightColor|nwn.get_area_light_color|pure|||||Areas and time||Gets the light color in the area specified. nColorType specifies the color type returned. Valid values for nColorType are the AREA_LIGHT_COLOR_* values. If no valid area (or object) is specified, it uses the area of caller. If an object other than an area is specified, will use the area that the object is currently in.|
function|GetAreaNoRestFlag|nwn.get_area_no_rest_flag|pure|||get_area_no_rest_flag||Areas and time||Gets the NoRest area flag. Returns TRUE if resting is not allowed in the area. Passing in OBJECT_INVALID to parameter oArea will result in operating on the area of the caller.|
function|GetAreaSize|nwn.get_area_size|pure|||||Areas and time||Gets the size of the area. - nAreaDimension: The area dimension that you wish to determine. AREA_HEIGHT AREA_WIDTH - oArea: The area that you wish to get the size of. Returns: The number of tiles that the area is wide/high, or zero on an error. If no valid area (or object) is specified, it uses the area of the caller. If an object other than an area is specified, will use the area that the object is currently in.|
function|GetAssociate|nwn.get_associate|pure|||||Creatures||Get the associate of type nAssociateType belonging to oMaster. - nAssociateType: ASSOCIATE_TYPE_* - nMaster - nTh: Which associate of the specified type to return * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if no such associate exists.|
function|GetAssociateType|nwn.get_associate_type|pure|||get_associate_type||Creatures||Returns the associate type of the specified creature. - Returns ASSOCIATE_TYPE_NONE if the creature is not the associate of anyone.|
function|GetAttackTarget|nwn.get_attack_target|pure|||get_attack_target||Creatures||Get the attack target of oCreature. This only works when oCreature is in combat.|
function|GetAttacksPerRound|nwn.get_attacks_per_round|pure||bCheckOverridenValue:Bool|get_attacks_per_round||Creatures||Gets the base number of attacks oCreature can make every round Excludes additional effects such as haste, slow, spells, circle kick, attack modes, etc. * bCheckOverridenValue - Checks for SetBaseAttackBonus() on the creature, if FALSE will return the non-overriden version|
function|GetBaseAttackBonus|nwn.get_base_attack_bonus|pure|||get_base_attack_bonus||Creatures||Returns the base attach bonus for the given creature.|
function|GetBaseItemType|nwn.get_base_item_type|pure|||get_base_item_type||Items||Get the base item type (BASE_ITEM_*) of oItem. * Returns BASE_ITEM_INVALID if oItem is an invalid item.|
function|GetCalendarDay|nwn.get_calendar_day|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current calendar day.|
function|GetCalendarMonth|nwn.get_calendar_month|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current calendar month.|
function|GetCalendarYear|nwn.get_calendar_year|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current calendar year.|
function|GetCasterLevel|nwn.get_caster_level|pure|||get_caster_level||Objects||Get the caster level of an object. This is consistent with the caster level used when applying effects if OBJECT_SELF is used. - oObject: A creature will return the caster level of their currently cast spell or ability, or the item's caster level if an item was used A placeable will return an automatic caster level: floor(10, (spell innate level * 2) - 1) An Area of Effect object will return the caster level that was used to create the Area of Effect. * Return value on error, or if oObject has not yet cast a spell: 0;|
function|GetChallengeRating|nwn.get_challenge_rating|pure|||get_challenge_rating||Objects||Get oCreature's challenge rating. * Returns 0.0 if oCreature is invalid.|
function|GetClassByPosition|nwn.get_class_by_position|pure|||||Creatures||A creature can have up to three classes. This function determines the creature's class (CLASS_TYPE_*) based on nClassPosition. - nClassPosition: 1, 2 or 3 - oCreature * Returns CLASS_TYPE_INVALID if the oCreature does not have a class in nClassPosition (i.e. a single-class creature will only have a value in nClassLocation=1) or if oCreature is not a valid creature.|
function|GetColor|nwn.get_color|pure|||get_color||Objects||Get the Color of oObject from the color channel specified. - oObject: the object from which you are obtaining the color. Can be a creature that has color information (i.e. the playable races). - nColorChannel: The color channel that you want to get the color value of. COLOR_CHANNEL_SKIN COLOR_CHANNEL_HAIR COLOR_CHANNEL_TATTOO_1 COLOR_CHANNEL_TATTOO_2 * Returns -1 on error.|
function|GetCommandable|nwn.get_commandable|pure|Bool||get_commandable||Objects||Determine whether oTarget's action stack can be modified.|
function|GetCreatureBodyPart|nwn.get_creature_body_part|pure|||||Creatures||returns the model number being used for the body part and creature specified The model number returned is for the body part when the creature is not wearing armor (i.e. whether or not the creature is wearing armor does not affect the return value). Note: Only works on part based creatures, which is typically restricted to the playable races (unless some new part based custom content has been added to the module). returns CREATURE_PART_INVALID if used on a non-creature object, or if the creature does not use a part based model. - nPart (CREATURE_PART_*) CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_FOOT CREATURE_PART_LEFT_FOOT CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_SHIN CREATURE_PART_LEFT_SHIN CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_THIGH CREATURE_PART_LEFT_THIGH CREATURE_PART_PELVIS CREATURE_PART_TORSO CREATURE_PART_BELT CREATURE_PART_NECK CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_FOREARM CREATURE_PART_LEFT_FOREARM CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_BICEP CREATURE_PART_LEFT_BICEP CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_SHOULDER CREATURE_PART_LEFT_SHOULDER CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_HAND CREATURE_PART_LEFT_HAND CREATURE_PART_HEAD|
function|GetCreatureSize|nwn.get_creature_size|pure|||get_creature_size||Creatures||Get the size (CREATURE_SIZE_*) of oCreature.|
function|GetCreatureTailType|nwn.get_creature_tail_type|pure|||get_creature_tail_type||Creatures||returns the Tail type of the creature specified. CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_NONE CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_LIZARD CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_BONE CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_DEVIL returns CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_NONE if used on a non-creature object, if the creature has no Tail, or if the creature can not have its Tail type changed in the toolset.|
function|GetCreatureWingType|nwn.get_creature_wing_type|pure|||get_creature_wing_type||Creatures||returns the Wing type of the creature specified. CREATURE_WING_TYPE_NONE CREATURE_WING_TYPE_DEMON CREATURE_WING_TYPE_ANGEL CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BAT CREATURE_WING_TYPE_DRAGON CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BUTTERFLY CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BIRD returns CREATURE_WING_TYPE_NONE if used on a non-creature object, if the creature has no wings, or if the creature can not have its wing type changed in the toolset.|
function|GetCurrentAction|nwn.get_current_action|pure|||get_current_action||Objects||Get the current action (ACTION_*) that oObject is executing.|
function|GetCurrentHitPoints|nwn.get_current_hit_points|manual|||||Creatures|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetCreatureHPExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetDeity|nwn.get_deity|pure|||get_deity||Objects||Get the name of oCreature's deity. * Returns "" if oCreature is invalid (or if the deity name is blank for oCreature).|
function|GetDescription|nwn.get_description|pure||bOriginalDescription:Bool,bIdentifiedDescription:Bool|get_description||Objects||Get the description of oObject. - oObject: the object from which you are obtaining the description. Can be a creature, item, placeable, door, trigger or module object. - bOriginalDescription: if set to true any new description specified via a SetDescription scripting command is ignored and the original object's description is returned instead. - bIdentified: If oObject is an item, setting this to TRUE will return the identified description, setting this to FALSE will return the unidentified description. This flag has no effect on objects other than items.|
function|GetDistanceBetween|nwn.get_distance_between|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetDistanceBetweenExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetDistanceBetweenLocations|nwn.get_distance_between_locations|pure||lLocationA:Location,lLocationB:Location|get_distance_between_locations||Objects||Get the distance between lLocationA and lLocationB.|
function|GetDroppableFlag|nwn.get_droppable_flag|pure|Bool||get_droppable_flag||Objects||returns TRUE if the item CAN be dropped Droppable items will appear on a creature's remains when the creature is killed.|
function|GetEffectCasterLevel|nwn.get_effect_caster_level|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_caster_level||Effects||Returns the caster level of the creature who created the effect. - If not created by a creature, returns 0. - If created by a spell-like ability, returns 0.|
function|GetEffectCreator|nwn.get_effect_creator|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_creator||Effects||Get the object that created eEffect. * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if eEffect is not a valid effect.|
function|GetEffectDuration|nwn.get_effect_duration|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_duration||Effects||Returns the total duration of the effect in seconds. - Returns 0 if the duration type of the effect is not DURATION_TYPE_TEMPORARY.|
function|GetEffectDurationRemaining|nwn.get_effect_duration_remaining|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_duration_remaining||Effects||Returns the remaining duration of the effect in seconds. - Returns 0 if the duration type of the effect is not DURATION_TYPE_TEMPORARY.|
function|GetEffectDurationType|nwn.get_effect_duration_type|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_duration_type||Effects||Get the duration type (DURATION_TYPE_*) of eEffect. * Return value if eEffect is not valid: -1|
function|GetEffectFloat|nwn.get_effect_float|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_float||Effects||Get the float parameter of eEffect at nIndex. * nIndex bounds: 0 >= nIndex < 4. * Some experimentation will be needed to find the right index for the value you wish to determine. Returns: the value or 0.0f on error/when not set.|
function|GetEffectInteger|nwn.get_effect_integer|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_integer||Effects||Get the integer parameter of eEffect at nIndex. * nIndex bounds: 0 >= nIndex < 8. * Some experimentation will be needed to find the right index for the value you wish to determine. Returns: the value or 0 on error/when not set.|
function|GetEffectLinkId|nwn.get_effect_link_id|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_link_id||Effects||Returns the given effects Link ID. There is no guarantees about this identifier other than it is unique and the same for all effects linked to it.|
function|GetEffectObject|nwn.get_effect_object|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_object||Effects||Get the object parameter of eEffect at nIndex. * nIndex bounds: 0 >= nIndex < 4. * Some experimentation will be needed to find the right index for the value you wish to determine. Returns: the value or OBJECT_INVALID on error/when not set.|
function|GetEffectSpellId|nwn.get_effect_spell_id|pure||eSpellEffect:Effect|get_effect_spell_id||Effects||Get the spell (SPELL_*) that applied eSpellEffect. * Returns -1 if eSpellEffect was applied outside a spell script.|
function|GetEffectString|nwn.get_effect_string|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_string||Effects||Get the string parameter of eEffect at nIndex. * nIndex bounds: 0 >= nIndex < 6. * Some experimentation will be needed to find the right index for the value you wish to determine. Returns: the value or "" on error/when not set.|
function|GetEffectSubType|nwn.get_effect_sub_type|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_sub_type||Effects||Get the subtype (SUBTYPE_*) of eEffect. * Return value on error: 0|
function|GetEffectTag|nwn.get_effect_tag|pure||eEffect:Effect|get_effect_tag||Effects||Returns the string tag set for the provided effect. - If no tag has been set, returns an empty string.|
function|GetEffectType|nwn.get_effect_type|pure||eEffect:Effect,bAllTypes:Bool|get_effect_type||Effects||Get the effect type (EFFECT_TYPE_*) of eEffect. - bAllTypes: Set to TRUE to return additional values the game used to return EFFECT_INVALIDEFFECT for, specifically: EFFECT_TYPE: APPEAR, CUTSCENE_DOMINATED, DAMAGE, DEATH, DISAPPEAR, HEAL, HITPOINTCHANGEWHENDYING, KNOCKDOWN, MODIFYNUMATTACKS, SUMMON_CREATURE, TAUNT, WOUNDING * Return value if eEffect is invalid: EFFECT_INVALIDEFFECT|
function|GetFacing|nwn.get_facing|pure|||get_facing||Objects||Get the direction in which oTarget is facing, expressed as a float between 0.0f and 360.0f * Return value on error: -1.0f|
function|GetFacingFromLocation|nwn.get_facing_from_location|pure||lLocation:Location|get_facing||Objects||Get the orientation value from lLocation.|
function|GetFactionAverageGoodEvilAlignment|nwn.get_faction_average_good_evil_alignment|pure|||get_faction_average_good_evil_alignment||Creatures||Get an integer between 0 and 100 (inclusive) that represents the average good/evil alignment of oFactionMember's faction. * Return value on error: -1|
function|GetFactionAverageLawChaosAlignment|nwn.get_faction_average_law_chaos_alignment|pure|||get_faction_average_law_chaos_alignment||Creatures||Get an integer between 0 and 100 (inclusive) that represents the average law/chaos alignment of oFactionMember's faction. * Return value on error: -1|
function|GetFactionAverageLevel|nwn.get_faction_average_level|pure|||get_faction_average_level||Creatures||Get the average level of the members of the faction. * Return value on error: -1|
function|GetFactionAverageReputation|nwn.get_faction_average_reputation|pure|||get_faction_average_reputation||Creatures||Get an integer between 0 and 100 (inclusive) that represents how oSourceFactionMember's faction feels about oTarget. * Return value on error: -1|
function|GetFactionAverageXP|nwn.get_faction_average_xp|pure|||get_faction_average_xp||Creatures||Get the average XP of the members of the faction. * Return value on error: -1|
function|GetFactionBestAC|nwn.get_faction_best_ac|pure||bMustBeVisible:Bool|get_faction_best_ac||Creatures||Get the object faction member with the highest armour class. * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if oFactionMember's faction is invalid.|
