function|GetMaxHitPoints|nwn.get_max_hit_points|manual|||||Creatures|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetCreatureHPExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetMemorizedSpellId|nwn.get_memorized_spell_id|pure|||get_memorized_spell_id||Creatures||Gets the spell id of a memorized spell slot. - nClassType: a CLASS_TYPE_* constant. Must be a MemorizesSpells class. - nSpellLevel: the spell level, 0-9. - nIndex: the index of the spell slot. Bounds: 0 <= nIndex < GetMemorizedSpellCountByLevel() Returns: a SPELL_* constant or -1 if the slot is not set.|
function|GetMemorizedSpellReady|nwn.get_memorized_spell_ready|pure|||get_memorized_spell_ready||Creatures||Gets the ready state of a memorized spell slot. - nClassType: a CLASS_TYPE_* constant. Must be a MemorizesSpells class. - nSpellLevel: the spell level, 0-9. - nIndex: the index of the spell slot. Bounds: 0 <= nIndex < GetMemorizedSpellCountByLevel() Returns: TRUE/FALSE or -1 if the slot is not set.|
function|GetModule|nwn.get_module|pure|||||Objects||Get the module. * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetModuleName|nwn.get_module_name|pure|||||Objects||Get the module's name in the language of the server that's running it. * If there is no entry for the language of the server, it will return an empty string|
function|GetMovementRate|nwn.get_movement_rate|pure|||get_movement_rate||Objects||Get oCreature's movement rate. * Returns 0 if oCreature is invalid.|
function|GetName|nwn.get_name|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetCreatureNameExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetNearestCreature|nwn.get_nearest_creature|pure|||||Creatures||Get the creature nearest to oTarget, subject to all the criteria specified. - nFirstCriteriaType: CREATURE_TYPE_* - nFirstCriteriaValue: -> CLASS_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_CLASS -> SPELL_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_DOES_NOT_HAVE_SPELL_EFFECT or CREATURE_TYPE_HAS_SPELL_EFFECT -> TRUE or FALSE if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_IS_ALIVE -> PERCEPTION_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_PERCEPTION -> PLAYER_CHAR_IS_PC or PLAYER_CHAR_NOT_PC if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_PLAYER_CHAR -> RACIAL_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_RACIAL_TYPE -> REPUTATION_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_REPUTATION For example, to get the nearest PC, use: (CREATURE_TYPE_PLAYER_CHAR, PLAYER_CHAR_IS_PC) - oTarget: We're trying to find the creature of the specified type that is nearest to oTarget - nNth: We don't have to find the first nearest: we can find the Nth nearest... - nSecondCriteriaType: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaType to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nSecondCriteriaValue: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaValue to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nThirdCriteriaType: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaType to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nThirdCriteriaValue: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaValue to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetNearestCreatureToLocation|nwn.get_nearest_creature_to_location|pure||lLocation:Location|||Creatures||Get the creature nearest to lLocation, subject to all the criteria specified. - nFirstCriteriaType: CREATURE_TYPE_* - nFirstCriteriaValue: -> CLASS_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_CLASS -> SPELL_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_DOES_NOT_HAVE_SPELL_EFFECT or CREATURE_TYPE_HAS_SPELL_EFFECT -> TRUE or FALSE if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_IS_ALIVE -> PERCEPTION_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_PERCEPTION -> PLAYER_CHAR_IS_PC or PLAYER_CHAR_NOT_PC if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_PLAYER_CHAR -> RACIAL_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_RACIAL_TYPE -> REPUTATION_TYPE_* if nFirstCriteriaType was CREATURE_TYPE_REPUTATION For example, to get the nearest PC, use (CREATURE_TYPE_PLAYER_CHAR, PLAYER_CHAR_IS_PC) - lLocation: We're trying to find the creature of the specified type that is nearest to lLocation - nNth: We don't have to find the first nearest: we can find the Nth nearest.... - nSecondCriteriaType: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaType to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nSecondCriteriaValue: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaValue to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nThirdCriteriaType: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaType to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. - nThirdCriteriaValue: This is used in the same way as nFirstCriteriaValue to further specify the type of creature that we are looking for. * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetNearestObject|nwn.get_nearest_object_by_type|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Nwn.NearestObjectExecutor|Explicit origin and OBJECT_TYPE mask, preserving legacy string-based Object.nearest_object_by_type separately.|
function|GetNearestObjectByTag|nwn.get_nearest_object_by_tag|pure|||||Objects||Get the nth Object nearest to oTarget that has sTag as its tag. * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetNearestObjectToLocation|nwn.get_nearest_object_to_location|pure||lLocation:Location|||Objects||Get the nNth object nearest to lLocation that is of the specified type. - nObjectType: OBJECT_TYPE_* - lLocation - nNth * Return value on error: OBJECT_INVALID|
function|GetNearestTrapToObject|nwn.get_nearest_trap_to_object|pure|||get_nearest_trap_to_object||Objects||Get the trap nearest to oTarget. Note : "trap objects" are actually any trigger, placeable or door that is trapped in oTarget's area. - oTarget - nTrapDetected: if this is TRUE, the trap returned has to have been detected by oTarget.|
function|GetObjectByTag|nwn.get_object_by_tag|pure|||||Objects||Get the nNth object with the specified tag. - sTag - nNth: the nth object with this tag may be requested * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if the object cannot be found. Note: The module cannot be retrieved by GetObjectByTag(), use GetModule() instead.|
function|GetObjectByUUID|nwn.get_object_by_uuid|pure|||||Objects||Looks up a object on the server by it's UUID. Returns OBJECT_INVALID if the UUID is not on the server.|
function|GetObjectType|nwn.get_object_type|pure|||get_object_type||Objects||Get the object type (OBJECT_TYPE_*) of oTarget * Return value if oTarget is not a valid object: -1|
function|GetObjectVisualTransform|nwn.get_object_visual_transform|pure||bCurrentLerp:Bool|get_object_visual_transform||Objects||Gets a visual transform on the given object. - oObject can be any valid Creature, Placeable, Item or Door. - nTransform is one of OBJECT_VISUAL_TRANSFORM_* - nScope is one of OBJECT_VISUAL_TRANSFORM_DATA_SCOPE_* and specific to the object type being VT'ed. Returns the current (or default) value.|
function|GetPickpocketableFlag|nwn.get_pickpocketable_flag|pure|Bool||get_pickpocketable_flag||Objects||returns TRUE if the item CAN be pickpocketed|
function|GetPlotFlag|nwn.get_plot_flag|pure|Bool||get_plot_flag||Objects||Determine whether oTarget is a plot object.|
function|GetPortraitId|nwn.get_portrait_id|pure|||get_portrait_id||Objects||Get the PortraitId of oTarget. - oTarget: the object for which you are getting the portrait Id. Returns: The Portrait Id number being used for the object oTarget. The Portrait Id refers to the row number of the Portraits.2da that this portrait is from. If a custom portrait is being used, oTarget is a player object, or on an error returns PORTRAIT_INVALID. In these instances try using GetPortraitResRef() instead.|
function|GetPortraitResRef|nwn.get_portrait_res_ref|pure|||get_portrait_res_ref||Objects||Get the Portrait ResRef of oTarget. - oTarget: the object for which you are getting the portrait ResRef. Returns: The Portrait ResRef being used for the object oTarget. The Portrait ResRef will not include a trailing size letter.|
function|GetPositionFromLocation|nwn.location_x|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Nwn.LocationCoordinateExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetRacialType|nwn.get_racial_type|manual|||||Creatures|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetCreatureRaceExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetReflexSavingThrow|nwn.get_reflex_saving_throw|pure|||get_reflex_saving_throw||Creatures||Get oTarget's base reflex saving throw value (this will only work for creatures, doors, and placeables). * Returns 0 if oTarget is invalid.|
function|GetResRef|nwn.get_resref|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetObjectResRefExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetSkillRank|nwn.get_skill_rank|pure|||||Creatures||Get the number of ranks that oTarget has in nSkill. - nSkill: SKILL_* - oTarget - nBaseSkillRank: if set to true returns the number of base skill ranks the target has (i.e. not including any bonuses from ability scores, feats, etc). * Returns -1 if oTarget doesn't have nSkill. * Returns 0 if nSkill is untrained.|
function|GetSpellResistance|nwn.get_spell_resistance|pure|||get_spell_resistance||Creatures||Returns the spell resistance of the specified creature. - Returns 0 if the creature has no spell resistance or an invalid creature is passed in.|
function|GetStolenFlag|nwn.get_stolen_flag|pure|Bool||get_stolen_flag||Objects||returns TRUE if the item is stolen|
function|GetStoreGold|nwn.get_store_gold|pure|||get_store_gold||Items||Returns the amount of gold a store currently has. -1 indicates it is not using gold. -2 indicates the store could not be located.|
function|GetStoreIdentifyCost|nwn.get_store_identify_cost|pure|||get_store_identify_cost||Items||Gets the amount a store charges for identifying an item. Default is 100. -1 means the store will not identify items. -2 indicates the store could not be located.|
function|GetStoreMaxBuyPrice|nwn.get_store_max_buy_price|pure|||get_store_max_buy_price||Items||Gets the maximum amount a store will pay for any item. -1 means price unlimited. -2 indicates the store could not be located.|
function|GetSubRace|nwn.get_sub_race|pure|||get_sub_race||Objects||Get the name of oCreature's sub race. * Returns "" if oCreature is invalid (or if sub race is blank for oCreature).|
function|GetTag|nwn.get_tag|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Getters.GetTagExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|GetTimeHour|nwn.get_time_hour|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current hour.|
function|GetTimeMinute|nwn.get_time_minute|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current minute|
function|GetTimeSecond|nwn.get_time_second|pure|||||Areas and time||Get the current second|
function|GetTransitionTarget|nwn.get_transition_target|pure|||get_transition_target||Objects||Get the destination object for the given object. All objects can hold a transition target, but only Doors and Triggers will be made clickable by the game engine (This may change in the future). You can set and query transition targets on other objects for your own scripted purposes. * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if oTransition does not hold a target.|
function|GetUseableFlag|nwn.get_useable_flag|pure|Bool||get_useable_flag||Objects||returns TRUE if the object is usable|
function|GetWaypointByTag|nwn.get_waypoint_by_tag|pure|||||Objects||Get the first waypoint with the specified tag. * Returns OBJECT_INVALID if the waypoint cannot be found.|
function|GetWeather|nwn.get_weather|pure|||get_weather||Areas and time||Gets the current weather conditions for the area oArea. Returns: WEATHER_CLEAR, WEATHER_RAIN, WEATHER_SNOW, WEATHER_INVALID Note: If called on an Interior area, this will always return WEATHER_CLEAR.|
function|GetWeight|nwn.get_weight|pure|||get_weight||Objects||Gets the weight of an item, or the total carried weight of a creature in tenths of pounds (as per the baseitems.2da). - oTarget: the item or creature for which the weight is needed|
function|GetWillSavingThrow|nwn.get_will_saving_throw|pure|||get_will_saving_throw||Creatures||Get oTarget's base will saving throw value (this will only work for creatures, doors, and placeables). * Returns 0 if oTarget is invalid.|
function|GetXP|nwn.get_xp|pure|||get_xp||Creatures||Get oCreature's experience.|
function|GiveGoldToCreature|nwn.give_gold_to_creature|action|||give_gold_to_creature||Creatures||Give nGP gold to oCreature.|
function|GiveXPToCreature|nwn.give_xp_to_creature|action|||give_xp_to_creature||Creatures||Gives nXpAmount to oCreature.|
function|JumpToLocation|nwn.jump_to_location|command||lDestination:Location|jump_to_location||Actions||Jump to lDestination. The action is added to the TOP of the action queue.|
function|JumpToObject|nwn.jump_to_object|command|||jump_to_object||Actions||Jump to oToJumpTo (the action is added to the top of the action queue).|
function|Location|nwn.location|manual|Location||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Nwn.LocationExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|MagicalEffect|nwn.magical_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|magical_effect||Effects||Set the subtype of eEffect to Magical and return eEffect. (Effects default to magical if the subtype is not set) Magical effects are removed by resting, and by dispel magic|
function|MusicBackgroundChangeDay|nwn.music_background_change_day|action|||music_background_change_day||Areas and time||Change the background day track for oArea to nTrack. - oArea - nTrack|
function|MusicBackgroundChangeNight|nwn.music_background_change_night|action|||music_background_change_night||Areas and time||Change the background night track for oArea to nTrack. - oArea - nTrack|
function|MusicBackgroundPlay|nwn.music_background_play|action|||music_background_play||Areas and time||Play the background music for oArea.|
function|MusicBackgroundStop|nwn.music_background_stop|action|||music_background_stop||Areas and time||Stop the background music for oArea.|
function|MusicBattleChange|nwn.music_battle_change|action|||music_battle_change||Areas and time||Change the battle track for oArea. - oArea - nTrack|
function|MusicBattlePlay|nwn.music_battle_play|action|||music_battle_play||Areas and time||Play the battle music for oArea.|
function|MusicBattleStop|nwn.music_battle_stop|action|||music_battle_stop||Areas and time||Stop the battle music for oArea.|
function|PlayAnimation|nwn.play_animation|command|||play_animation||Actions||Play nAnimation immediately. - nAnimation: ANIMATION_* - fSpeed - fSeconds|
function|PlaySound|nwn.play_sound|command|||play_sound||Objects||Play sSoundName - sSoundName: TBD - SS This will play a mono sound from the location of the object running the command.|
function|RemoveEffect|nwn.remove_effect|action||eEffect:Effect|remove_effect||Effects||Remove eEffect from oCreature. * No return value|
function|RemoveHenchman|nwn.remove_henchman|action|||remove_henchman||Objects||Remove oHenchman from the service of oMaster, returning them to their original faction.|
function|RemoveJournalQuestEntry|nwn.remove_journal_quest_entry|action||bAllPartyMembers:Bool,bAllPlayers:Bool|||Objects||Remove a journal quest entry from oCreature. - szPlotID: the plot identifier used in the toolset's Journal Editor - oCreature - bAllPartyMembers: If this is TRUE, the entry will be removed from the journal of everyone in the party - bAllPlayers: If this is TRUE, the entry will be removed from the journal of everyone in the world|
function|RestoreCameraFacing|nwn.restore_camera_facing|action|||||Objects||Restores the camera mode and position to what they were last time StoreCameraFacing was called. RestoreCameraFacing can only be called once, and must correspond to a previous call to StoreCameraFacing.|
function|SendMessageToAllDMs|nwn.send_message_to_all_d_ms|action|||||Objects||Sends szMessage to all the Dungeon Masters currently on the server.|
function|SendMessageToPC|nwn.send_message_to_pc|action|||send_message_to_pc||Objects||Send a server message (szMessage) to the oPlayer.|
function|SetAILevel|nwn.set_ai_level|action|||set_ai_level||Objects||Sets the current AI Level of the creature to the value specified. Does not work on Players. The game by default will choose an appropriate AI level for creatures based on the circumstances that the creature is in. Explicitly setting an AI level will over ride the game AI settings. The new setting will last until SetAILevel is called again with the argument AI_LEVEL_DEFAULT. AI_LEVEL_DEFAULT - Default setting. The game will take over seting the appropriate AI level when required. AI_LEVEL_VERY_LOW - Very Low priority, very stupid, but low CPU usage for AI. Typically used when no players are in the area. AI_LEVEL_LOW - Low priority, mildly stupid, but slightly more CPU usage for AI. Typically used when not in combat, but a player is in the area. AI_LEVEL_NORMAL - Normal priority, average AI, but more CPU usage required for AI. Typically used when creature is in combat. AI_LEVEL_HIGH - High priority, smartest AI, but extremely high CPU usage required for AI. Avoid using this. It is most likely only ever needed for cutscenes.|
function|SetActionMode|nwn.set_action_mode|action|||set_action_mode||Objects||Sets the status of modes ACTION_MODE_* on a creature.|
function|SetAreaNoRestFlag|nwn.set_area_no_rest_flag|action||bNoRestFlag:Bool|||Areas and time||Sets the NoRest flag on an area. Passing in OBJECT_INVALID to parameter oArea will result in operating on the area of the caller.|
function|SetBaseAttackBonus|nwn.set_base_attack_bonus|action|||||Creatures||Sets the number of base attacks each round for the specified creature (PC or NPC). If set on a PC it will not be shown on their character sheet, but will save to BIC/savegame. - nBaseAttackBonus - Number of base attacks per round, 1 to 6|
function|SetCalendar|nwn.set_calendar|action|||||Areas and time||Set the calendar to the specified date. - nYear should be from 0 to 32000 inclusive - nMonth should be from 1 to 12 inclusive - nDay should be from 1 to 28 inclusive 1) Time can only be advanced forwards; attempting to set the time backwards will result in no change to the calendar. 2) If values larger than the month or day are specified, they will be wrapped around and the overflow will be used to advance the next field. e.g. Specifying a year of 1350, month of 33 and day of 10 will result in the calender being set to a year of 1352, a month of 9 and a day of 10.|
function|SetCameraFacing|nwn.set_camera_facing|action|||||Objects||Change the direction in which the camera is facing - fDirection is expressed as anticlockwise degrees from Due East. (0.0f=East, 90.0f=North, 180.0f=West, 270.0f=South) A value of -1.0f for any parameter will be ignored and instead it will use the current camera value. This can be used to change the way the camera is facing after the player emerges from an area transition. - nTransitionType: CAMERA_TRANSITION_TYPE_* SNAP will immediately move the camera to the new position, while the other types will result in the camera moving gradually into position Pitch and distance are limited to valid values for the current camera mode: Top Down: Distance = 5-20, Pitch = 1-50 Driving camera: Distance = 6 (can't be changed), Pitch = 1-62 Chase: Distance = 5-20, Pitch = 1-50 *** NOTE *** In NWN:Hordes of the Underdark the camera limits have been relaxed to the following: Distance 1-25 Pitch 1-89|
function|SetCameraHeight|nwn.set_camera_height|action|||set_camera_height||Objects||Forces this player's camera to be set to this height. Setting this value to zero will restore the camera to the racial default height.|
function|SetCameraMode|nwn.set_camera_mode|action|||set_camera_mode||Objects||Set the camera mode for oPlayer. - oPlayer - nCameraMode: CAMERA_MODE_* * If oPlayer is not player-controlled or nCameraMode is invalid, nothing happens.|
function|SetColor|nwn.set_color|action|||set_color||Objects||Set the color channel of oObject to the color specified. - oObject: the object for which you are changing the color. Can be a creature that has color information (i.e. the playable races). - nColorChannel: The color channel that you want to set the color value of. COLOR_CHANNEL_SKIN COLOR_CHANNEL_HAIR COLOR_CHANNEL_TATTOO_1 COLOR_CHANNEL_TATTOO_2 - nColorValue: The color you want to set (0-175).|
function|SetCommandable|nwn.set_commandable|action||bCommandable:Bool|||Objects||Set whether oTarget's action stack can be modified|
function|SetCreatureAppearanceType|nwn.set_creature_appearance_type|action|||set_creature_appearance_type||Creatures||Sets the creature's appearance type to the value specified (uses the APPEARANCE_TYPE_XXX constants)|
function|SetCreatureBodyPart|nwn.set_creature_body_part|action|||||Creatures||Sets the body part model to be used on the creature specified. The model names for parts need to be in the following format: p<m/f><race letter><phenotype>_<body part><model number>.mdl - nPart (CREATURE_PART_*) CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_FOOT CREATURE_PART_LEFT_FOOT CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_SHIN CREATURE_PART_LEFT_SHIN CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_THIGH CREATURE_PART_LEFT_THIGH CREATURE_PART_PELVIS CREATURE_PART_TORSO CREATURE_PART_BELT CREATURE_PART_NECK CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_FOREARM CREATURE_PART_LEFT_FOREARM CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_BICEP CREATURE_PART_LEFT_BICEP CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_SHOULDER CREATURE_PART_LEFT_SHOULDER CREATURE_PART_RIGHT_HAND CREATURE_PART_LEFT_HAND CREATURE_PART_HEAD - nModelNumber: CREATURE_MODEL_TYPE_* CREATURE_MODEL_TYPE_NONE CREATURE_MODEL_TYPE_SKIN (not for use on shoulders, pelvis or head). CREATURE_MODEL_TYPE_TATTOO (for body parts that support tattoos, i.e. not heads/feet/hands). CREATURE_MODEL_TYPE_UNDEAD (undead model only exists for the right arm parts). - oCreature: the creature to change the body part for. Note: Only part based creature appearance types are supported. i.e. The model types for the playable races ('P') in the appearance.2da|
function|SetCreatureTailType|nwn.set_creature_tail_type|action|||||Creatures||Sets the Tail type of the creature specified. - nTailType (CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_*) CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_NONE CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_LIZARD CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_BONE CREATURE_TAIL_TYPE_DEVIL - oCreature: the creature to change the Tail type for. Note: Only two creature model types will support Tails. The MODELTYPE for the part based (playable) races 'P' and MODELTYPE 'T'in the appearance.2da|
function|SetCreatureWingType|nwn.set_creature_wing_type|action|||||Creatures||Sets the Wing type of the creature specified. - nWingType (CREATURE_WING_TYPE_*) CREATURE_WING_TYPE_NONE CREATURE_WING_TYPE_DEMON CREATURE_WING_TYPE_ANGEL CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BAT CREATURE_WING_TYPE_DRAGON CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BUTTERFLY CREATURE_WING_TYPE_BIRD - oCreature: the creature to change the wing type for. Note: Only two creature model types will support wings. The MODELTYPE for the part based (playable races) 'P' and MODELTYPE 'W'in the appearance.2da|
function|SetDescription|nwn.set_description|action||bIdentifiedDescription:Bool|set_description||Objects||Set the description of oObject. - oObject: the object for which you are changing the description Can be a creature, placeable, item, door, or trigger. - sNewDescription: the new description that the object will use. - bIdentified: If oObject is an item, setting this to TRUE will set the identified description, setting this to FALSE will set the unidentified description. This flag has no effect on objects other than items. Note: Setting an object's description to "" will make the object revert to using the description it originally had before any SetDescription() calls were made on the object.|
function|SetDroppableFlag|nwn.set_droppable_flag|action||bDroppable:Bool|set_droppable_flag||Objects||Sets the droppable flag on an item - oItem: the item to change - bDroppable: TRUE or FALSE, whether the item should be droppable Droppable items will appear on a creature's remains when the creature is killed.|
function|SetEffectCreator|nwn.set_effect_creator|action|Effect|eEffect:Effect|set_effect_creator||Effects||Sets the effect creator - oCreator: The creator of the effect. Can be OBJECT_INVALID.|
function|SetEffectSpellId|nwn.set_effect_spell_id|action|Effect|eEffect:Effect|set_effect_spell_id||Effects||Sets the effect spell id - nSpellId: The spell id for the purposes of effect stacking, dispel magic and GetEffectSpellId. Must be >= -1 (-1 being invalid/no spell)|
function|SetEncounterActive|nwn.set_encounter_active|action|||||Objects||Set oEncounter's active state to nNewValue. - nNewValue: TRUE/FALSE - oEncounter|
function|SetEncounterDifficulty|nwn.set_encounter_difficulty|action|||||Objects||Set the difficulty level of oEncounter. - nEncounterDifficulty: ENCOUNTER_DIFFICULTY_* - oEncounter|
function|SetEncounterSpawnsCurrent|nwn.set_encounter_spawns_current|action|||||Objects||Set the number of times that oEncounter has spawned so far|
function|SetEncounterSpawnsMax|nwn.set_encounter_spawns_max|action|||||Objects||Set the maximum number of times that oEncounter can spawn|
function|SetFacing|nwn.set_facing|action|||||Objects||Cause oObject to face fDirection. - fDirection is expressed as anticlockwise degrees from Due East. DIRECTION_EAST, DIRECTION_NORTH, DIRECTION_WEST and DIRECTION_SOUTH are predefined. (0.0f=East, 90.0f=North, 180.0f=West, 270.0f=South)|
function|SetFogAmount|nwn.set_fog_amount|action|||||Areas and time||Sets the fog amount in the area specified. nFogType = FOG_TYPE_* specifies wether the Sun, Moon, or both fog types are set. nFogAmount = specifies the density that the fog is being set to. If no valid area (or object) is specified, it uses the area of caller. If an object other than an area is specified, will use the area that the object is currently in.|
function|SetFogColor|nwn.set_fog_color|action|||||Areas and time||Sets the fog color in the area specified. nFogType = FOG_TYPE_* specifies wether the Sun, Moon, or both fog types are set. nFogColor = FOG_COLOR_* specifies the color the fog is being set to. The fog color can also be represented as a hex RGB number if specific color shades are desired. The format of a hex specified color would be 0xFFEEDD where FF would represent the amount of red in the color EE would represent the amount of green in the color DD would represent the amount of blue in the color. If no valid area (or object) is specified, it uses the area of caller. If an object other than an area is specified, will use the area that the object is currently in. If fFadeTime is above 0.0, it will fade to the new color in the amount of seconds specified.|
function|SetGender|nwn.set_gender|action|||set_gender||Creatures||Set the gender of oCreature. - nGender: a GENDER_* constant.|
function|SetHardness|nwn.set_hardness|action|||||Objects||Sets the Hardness of a Door or Placeable object. - nHardness: must be between 0 and 250. - oObject: a door or placeable object. Does nothing if used on an object that is neither a door nor a placeable.|
function|SetIdentified|nwn.set_identified|action||bIdentified:Bool|set_identified||Objects||Set whether oItem has been identified.|
function|SetImmortal|nwn.set_immortal|action||bImmortal:Bool|set_immortal||Objects||Set a creature's immortality flag. -oCreature: creature affected -bImmortal: TRUE = creature is immortal and cannot be killed (but still takes damage) FALSE = creature is not immortal and is damaged normally. This scripting command only works on Creature objects.|
function|SetInfiniteFlag|nwn.set_infinite_flag|action||bInfinite:Bool|set_infinite_flag||Objects||Sets the Infinite flag on an item - oItem: the item to change - bInfinite: TRUE or FALSE, whether the item should be Infinite The infinite property affects the buying/selling behavior of the item in a store. An infinite item will still be available to purchase from a store after a player buys the item (non-infinite items will disappear from the store when purchased).|
function|SetIsDestroyable|nwn.set_is_destroyable|action||bDestroyable:Bool,bRaiseable:Bool,bSelectableWhenDead:Bool|||Objects||Set the destroyable status of oObject - bDestroyable: If this is FALSE, the caller does not fade out on death, but sticks around as a corpse. - bRaiseable: If this is TRUE, the caller can be raised via resurrection. - bSelectableWhenDead: If this is TRUE, the caller is selectable after death. - oObject: Object to affect.|
function|SetItemCharges|nwn.set_item_charges|action|||set_item_charges||Items||Sets charges left on an item. - oItem: item to change - nCharges: number of charges. If value below 0 is passed, # charges will be set to 0. If value greater than maximum is passed, # charges will be set to maximum. If the # charges drops to 0 the item will be destroyed.|
function|SetItemCursedFlag|nwn.set_item_cursed_flag|action|||set_item_cursed_flag||Items||When cursed, items cannot be dropped|
function|SetItemStackSize|nwn.set_item_stack_size|action|||set_item_stack_size||Items||Sets stack size of an item. - oItem: item to change - nSize: new size of stack. Will be restricted to be between 1 and the maximum stack size for the item type. If a value less than 1 is passed it will set the stack to 1. If a value greater than the max is passed then it will set the stack to the maximum size|
function|SetLocalFloat|nwn.set_local_float|action|||set_local_float||Locals||Set oObject's local float variable sVarName to nValue|
function|SetLocalInt|nwn.set_local_int|action|||set_local_int||Locals||Set oObject's local integer variable sVarName to nValue|
function|SetLocalLocation|nwn.set_local_location|action||lValue:Location|set_local_location||Locals||Set oObject's local location variable sVarname to lValue|
function|SetLocalObject|nwn.set_local_object|action|||set_local_object||Locals||Set oObject's local object variable sVarName to nValue|
function|SetLocalString|nwn.set_local_string|action|||set_local_string||Locals||Set oObject's local string variable sVarName to nValue|
function|SetLockKeyRequired|nwn.set_lock_key_required|action|||set_lock_key_required||Objects||When set the object can not be opened unless the opener possesses the required key. The key tag required can be specified either in the toolset, or by using the SetLockKeyTag() scripting command. - oObject: a door, or placeable. - nKeyRequired: TRUE/FALSE|
function|SetLockKeyTag|nwn.set_lock_key_tag|action|||set_lock_key_tag||Objects||Set the key tag required to open object oObject. This will only have an effect if the object is set to "Key required to unlock or lock" either in the toolset or by using the scripting command SetLockKeyRequired(). - oObject: a door, placeable or trigger. - sNewKeyTag: the key tag required to open the locked object.|
function|SetLockLockDC|nwn.set_lock_lock_dc|action|||set_lock_lock_dc||Objects||Sets the DC for locking the object. - oObject: a door or placeable object. - nNewLockDC: must be between 0 and 250.|
function|SetLockLockable|nwn.set_lock_lockable|action|||set_lock_lockable||Objects||Sets whether or not the object can be locked. - oObject: a door or placeable. - nLockable: TRUE/FALSE|
function|SetLockUnlockDC|nwn.set_lock_unlock_dc|action|||set_lock_unlock_dc||Objects||Sets the DC for unlocking the object. - oObject: a door or placeable object. - nNewUnlockDC: must be between 0 and 250.|
function|SetLocked|nwn.set_locked|action||bLocked:Bool|set_locked||Objects||Set the locked state of oTarget, which can be a door or a placeable object.|
function|SetMapPinEnabled|nwn.set_map_pin_enabled|action|||set_map_pin_enabled||Objects||Set whether oMapPin is enabled. - oMapPin - nEnabled: 0=Off, 1=On|
function|SetName|nwn.set_name|manual|||||Objects|AmiaReforged.PwEngine.Features.Glyph.Runtime.Nodes.Actions.SetCreatureNameExecutor|Explicit adapter preserving runtime semantics and published identities.|
function|SetObjectVisualTransform|nwn.set_object_visual_transform|action||bPauseWithGame:Bool|set_object_visual_transform||Objects||Sets a visual transform on the given object. - oObject can be any valid Creature, Placeable, Item or Door. - nTransform is one of OBJECT_VISUAL_TRANSFORM_* - fValue depends on the transformation to apply. - nScope is one of OBJECT_VISUAL_TRANSFORM_DATA_SCOPE_* and specific to the object type being VT'ed. - nBehaviorFlags: bitmask of OBJECT_VISUAL_TRANSFORM_BEHAVIOR_*. - nRepeats: If > 0: N times, jump back to initial/from state after completing the transform. If -1: Do forever. Returns the old/previous value.|
function|SetPickpocketableFlag|nwn.set_pickpocketable_flag|action||bPickpocketable:Bool|set_pickpocketable_flag||Objects||Sets the Pickpocketable flag on an item - oItem: the item to change - bPickpocketable: TRUE or FALSE, whether the item can be pickpocketed.|
function|SetPlotFlag|nwn.set_plot_flag|action|||set_plot_flag||Objects||Set oTarget's plot object status.|
function|SetPortraitId|nwn.set_portrait_id|action|||set_portrait_id||Objects||Change the portrait of oTarget to use the Portrait Id specified. - oTarget: the object for which you are changing the portrait. - nPortraitId: The Id of the new portrait to use. nPortraitId refers to a row in the Portraits.2da Note: Not all portrait Ids are suitable for use with all object types. Setting the portrait Id will also cause the portrait ResRef to be set to the appropriate portrait ResRef for the Id specified.|
function|SetPortraitResRef|nwn.set_portrait_res_ref|action|||set_portrait_res_ref||Objects||Change the portrait of oTarget to use the Portrait ResRef specified. - oTarget: the object for which you are changing the portrait. - sPortraitResRef: The ResRef of the new portrait to use. The ResRef should not include any trailing size letter ( e.g. po_el_f_09_ ). Note: Not all portrait ResRefs are suitable for use with all object types. Setting the portrait ResRef will also cause the portrait Id to be set to PORTRAIT_INVALID.|
function|SetStolenFlag|nwn.set_stolen_flag|action|||set_stolen_flag||Objects||Sets whether this item is 'stolen' or not|
function|SetStoreGold|nwn.set_store_gold|action|||set_store_gold||Items||Sets the amount of gold a store has. -1 means the store does not use gold.|
function|SetStoreIdentifyCost|nwn.set_store_identify_cost|action|||set_store_identify_cost||Items||Sets the amount a store charges for identifying an item. Default is 100. -1 means the store will not identify items.|
function|SetStoreMaxBuyPrice|nwn.set_store_max_buy_price|action|||set_store_max_buy_price||Items||Sets the maximum amount a store will pay for any item. -1 means price unlimited.|
function|SetTag|nwn.set_tag|action|||set_tag||Objects||Sets a new tag for oObject. Will do nothing for invalid objects or the module object. Note: Care needs to be taken with this function. Changing the tag for creature with waypoints will make them stop walking them. Changing waypoint, door or trigger tags will break their area transitions.|
function|SetTime|nwn.set_time|action|||||Areas and time||Set the time to the time specified. - nHour should be from 0 to 23 inclusive - nMinute should be from 0 to 59 inclusive - nSecond should be from 0 to 59 inclusive - nMillisecond should be from 0 to 999 inclusive 1) Time can only be advanced forwards; attempting to set the time backwards will result in the day advancing and then the time being set to that specified, e.g. if the current hour is 15 and then the hour is set to 3, the day will be advanced by 1 and the hour will be set to 3. 2) If values larger than the max hour, minute, second or millisecond are specified, they will be wrapped around and the overflow will be used to advance the next field, e.g. specifying 62 hours, 250 minutes, 10 seconds and 10 milliseconds will result in the calendar day being advanced by 2 and the time being set to 18 hours, 10 minutes, 10 milliseconds.|
function|SetTrapActive|nwn.set_trap_active|action|||set_trap_active||Objects||Sets whether or not the trap is an active trap - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nActive: TRUE/FALSE Notes: Setting a trap as inactive will not make the trap disappear if it has already been detected. Call SetTrapDetectedBy() to make a detected trap disappear. To make an inactive trap not detectable call SetTrapDetectable()|
function|SetTrapDetectDC|nwn.set_trap_detect_dc|action|||set_trap_detect_dc||Objects||Set the DC for detecting oTrapObject. - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nDetectDC: must be between 0 and 250.|
function|SetTrapDetectable|nwn.set_trap_detectable|action|||set_trap_detectable||Objects||Sets whether or not the trapped object can be detected. - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nDetectable: TRUE/FALSE Note: Setting a trapped object to not be detectable will not make the trap disappear if it has already been detected.|
function|SetTrapDetectedBy|nwn.set_trap_detected_by|action||bDetected:Bool|set_trap_detected_by||Objects||Set whether or not the creature oDetector has detected the trapped object oTrap. - oTrap: A trapped trigger, placeable or door object. - oDetector: This is the creature that the detected status of the trap is being adjusted for. - bDetected: A Boolean that sets whether the trapped object has been detected or not.|
function|SetTrapDisarmDC|nwn.set_trap_disarm_dc|action|||set_trap_disarm_dc||Objects||Set the DC for disarming oTrapObject. - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nDisarmDC: must be between 0 and 250.|
function|SetTrapDisarmable|nwn.set_trap_disarmable|action|||set_trap_disarmable||Objects||Sets whether or not the trapped object can be disarmed. - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nDisarmable: TRUE/FALSE|
function|SetTrapKeyTag|nwn.set_trap_key_tag|action|||set_trap_key_tag||Objects||Set the tag of the key that will disarm oTrapObject. - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger|
function|SetTrapOneShot|nwn.set_trap_one_shot|action|||set_trap_one_shot||Objects||Sets whether or not the trap is a one-shot trap (i.e. whether or not the trap resets itself after firing). - oTrapObject: a placeable, door or trigger - nOneShot: TRUE/FALSE|
function|SetUseableFlag|nwn.set_useable_flag|action|||set_useable_flag||Objects||Set oTarget's useable object status. Note: Only works on non-static placeables, creatures, doors and items. On items, it affects interactivity when they're on the ground, and not useability in inventory.|
function|SetWeather|nwn.set_weather|action|||set_weather||Areas and time||Set the weather for oTarget. - oTarget: if this is GetModule(), all outdoor areas will be modified by the weather constant. If it is an area, oTarget will play the weather only if it is an outdoor area. - nWeather: WEATHER_* -> WEATHER_USER_AREA_SETTINGS will set the area back to random weather. -> WEATHER_CLEAR, WEATHER_RAIN, WEATHER_SNOW will make the weather go to the appropriate precipitation *without stopping*.|
function|SetXP|nwn.set_xp|action|||set_xp||Creatures||Sets oCreature's experience to nXpAmount.|
function|SpeakString|nwn.speak_string|command|||speak_string||Actions||The caller will immediately speak sStringToSpeak (this is different from ActionSpeakString) - sStringToSpeak - nTalkVolume: TALKVOLUME_*|
function|SummonAnimalCompanion|nwn.summon_animal_companion|action|||summon_animal_companion||Objects||Summon an Animal Companion|
function|SummonFamiliar|nwn.summon_familiar|action|||summon_familiar||Objects||Summon a Familiar|
function|SupernaturalEffect|nwn.supernatural_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|supernatural_effect||Effects||Set the subtype of eEffect to Supernatural and return eEffect. (Effects default to magical if the subtype is not set) Permanent supernatural effects are not removed by resting|
function|TagEffect|nwn.tag_effect|action|Effect|eEffect:Effect|tag_effect||Effects||Tags the effect with the provided string. - Any other tags in the link will be overwritten.|
function|TakeGoldFromCreature|nwn.take_gold_from_creature|action||bDestroy:Bool|||Creatures||Take nAmount of gold from oCreatureToTakeFrom. - nAmount - oCreatureToTakeFrom: If this is not a valid creature, nothing will happen. - bDestroy: If this is TRUE, the caller will not get the gold. Instead, the gold will be destroyed and will vanish from the game.|
function|VersusAlignmentEffect|nwn.versus_alignment_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|versus_alignment_effect||Effects||Set eEffect to be versus a specific alignment. - eEffect - nLawChaos: ALIGNMENT_LAWFUL/ALIGNMENT_CHAOTIC/ALIGNMENT_ALL - nGoodEvil: ALIGNMENT_GOOD/ALIGNMENT_EVIL/ALIGNMENT_ALL|
function|VersusRacialTypeEffect|nwn.versus_racial_type_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|versus_racial_type_effect||Effects||Set eEffect to be versus nRacialType. - eEffect - nRacialType: RACIAL_TYPE_*|
function|VersusTrapEffect|nwn.versus_trap_effect|pure|Effect|eEffect:Effect|versus_trap_effect||Effects||Set eEffect to be versus traps.|
